    "title": "**Heading-in-list**",
    "text": "**Heading-in-list**: resolved — a block's title isn't limited to headings, which cap at H6 and don't fit an unbounded tree. Any block whose text opens with a colon-delimited lead-in term (`Term: rest of the text`) uses that term as its title; bold/`**...**` around the term is a free style choice, not part of the rule, and its `**` characters slugify like any other non-alphanumeric character if present, same as headings' `#` markers. List nesting carries unbounded depth the same way heading nesting carries bounded depth. See [Architecture](../design/linking.md#id/BlockNode:00CDBYV4T8002). The exact rule for which colon counts as the delimiter — outside bold *and* inline code, length-capped, language-dependent — was refined after live corpus ingestion surfaced real corruption from a simpler version of it; see [Lead-In Term Detection](../design/linking.md#id/BlockNode:00CDBYV4TG000).",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00CDBYV5A800A",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": [
      "BlockNode:00CJ3A8RT8001",
      "BlockNode:00CJ3A8RT8002"
    ]
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00CDBYV5A800D",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "links": [
      {
        "@id": "BlockNode:00CDBYV5A800D:links:Link:00CJ3C4SQG000",
        "@type": "Link",
        "target": "BlockNode:00CDBYV4T8007",
        "predicate": "[[wikilink]]",
        "props": [
          {
            "@id": "BlockNode:00CDBYV5A800D:links:Link:00CJ3C4SQG000:props:StringProp:00CJ3C4SQG001",
            "@type": "StringProp",
            "key": "position",
            "value": "334"
          }
        ]
      }
    ],
    "title": "**`[[deep-path]]` coexistence**",
    "text": "**`[[deep-path]]` coexistence**: not needed, at least for now — `aperas://` scheme URLs (in-app) and `#fragment`s (compatible/pre-ingestion), including an `id/<ID>` fragment form, already make an internal reference unambiguous without a `[[...]]` wrapper. See [Topology](../design/linking.md#id/BlockNode:00CDBYV4T8007).",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00CDBYV5A800A",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": [
      "BlockNode:00CJ3A8D0G001",
      "BlockNode:00CJ3A8D0G002"
    ]
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00CDBYV5A800E",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "links": [
      {
        "@id": "BlockNode:00CDBYV5A800E:links:Link:00CJ3C4HSG000",
        "@type": "Link",
        "target": "BlockNode:00CDBYV4T8002",
        "predicate": "[[wikilink]]",
