    ],
    "title": "**2026-09-10: Slice 2 landed**",
    "text": "**2026-09-10: Slice 2 landed**: completing the toolset for working directly on Apeiron, corpus-wide rollout left as its own separate topic. `apeironNgn/node.ts`'s `rejectSlugPathCollisions` now rejects a document at ingestion time if any block's full slug-path — or an embedded anchor name still on it — is already claimed by a different block, live or within the same fresh parse; a writer-facing hard reject only, no lifecycle tracking (see [Design](../design/linking.md#id/BlockNode:00CDBYV4TG006)). The cleanup pass turned out to need no new removal API at all: an `aperas-tree` anchor is derived fresh from source text on every ingestion, so deleting the tag from the file and re-ingesting is the whole mechanism — confirmed live once the actual safety check was corrected to a full-text corpus search rather than `kg:backlinks` (which only sees already-tracked referrers). Slice 1's own scratch-ingest verification, left pending since it landed, is folded into `verify.ts` as steps 13-15 alongside Slice 2's own new coverage. See [Discussion](../discussion/linking.md#id/BlockNode:00CDBZ76TR00C) for a real id-format bug this surfaced while landing.",
