      },
      {
        "@id": "BlockNode:00CDGTX55R002:props:StringProp:00CE598VC8001",
        "@type": "StringProp",
        "key": "startIndex",
        "value": "1"
      }
    ],
    "title": "`packages/core` — the ApeironNgn engine and markdown parsing",
    "text": "`packages/core` — the ApeironNgn engine and markdown parsing: `apeironNgn/*`, `astParser.ts`, `reconcile.ts`, `props.ts`, `project.ts`, `snowflake.ts`, `leadingPart.ts`, `nodeRef.ts`, `lineReader.ts`, `folders.ts`, `artifacts.ts`, `verify.ts`. No process/argv/RPC concerns.",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00CDGTX55R001",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": []
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00CDGTX55R003",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "title": "00CDGTX55R003",
    "text": "`packages/cli` — every `kgX.ts` command, `kgHelp.ts`, the service/RPC layer (`apeironNgn/service.ts`, `serviceClient.ts`, `serviceLock.ts`, `serviceProtocol.ts` — moving here since the service exists purely to let many short-lived CLI processes share one warm graph, a CLI concern, not a core one), and `apeironNgnSmokeTest.ts`. Depends on `core`.",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00CDGTX55R001",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": []
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00CDGTX55R004",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "title": "00CDGTX55R004",
    "text": "`packages/web` — the Solid/Vite app, stripped to a placeholder (its current content is 100% unmodified scaffold, never built out). Depends on `core`.",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00CDGTX55R001",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": []
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00CDGTX55R005",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "title": "00CDGTX55R005",
    "text": "Cross-package imports go through each package's own `exports` map (`\"./*\": \"./src/*.ts\"`), not relative dot-paths — `import ... from '@aperas/core/apeironNgn/node'` instead of `'../apeironNgn/node'` — resolved by npm workspace symlinking, the same subpath shape the code already uses today, so the rewrite is a mechanical prefix swap, not a redesign. Root `package.json` keeps the existing `kg:*` script names (pointing at their new `packages/cli/src/...` locations) so the dogfooding workflow (`npm run kg:X -- <args>`, now run from `Aperas/monorepo/`) is unchanged in shape. Two unused dependencies (`terminusdb`, `rehype-stringify`/`remark-rehype` — confirmed zero references anywhere in `src/`) are dropped rather than assigned to any package.",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00CDGTX55R001",
    "type": "paragraph",
    "children": []
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00CDGTZHSR001",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "title": "## Topology",
    "text": "An npm workspace under a renamed root (`Aperas/monorepo/`, replacing `Aperas/web/` — a directory called \"web\" stopped meaning \"the frontend\" once it also housed the whole engine and CLI), three packages:",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00CDDVBXH8001",
    "type": "heading",
    "children": [
      "BlockNode:00CDGTZHSR002",
      "BlockNode:00CDGTZHSR003",
      "BlockNode:00CDGTZHSR004",
      "BlockNode:00CDGTZHSR005"
    ]
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00CDGTZHSR002",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "title": "`packages/core` — the ApeironNgn engine and markdown parsing",
    "text": "`packages/core` — the ApeironNgn engine and markdown parsing: `apeironNgn/*` (everything except the service/RPC layer, which is CLI-scoped — see below), `astParser.ts`, `reconcile.ts`, `props.ts`, `project.ts`, `snowflake.ts`, `leadingPart.ts`, `nodeRef.ts`, `lineReader.ts`, `folders.ts`, `artifacts.ts`. No process/argv/RPC concerns.",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00CDGTZHSR001",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": []
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00CDGTZHSR003",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "title": "00CDGTZHSR003",
    "text": "`packages/cli` — every `kgX.ts` command, `kgHelp.ts`, the service/RPC layer (`apeironNgn/service.ts`, `serviceClient.ts`, `serviceLock.ts`, `serviceProtocol.ts`, `apeironNgn/codeVersion.ts` — moving here since the service exists purely to let many short-lived CLI processes share one warm graph, a CLI concern, not a core one), `apeironNgnSmokeTest.ts`, and `verify.ts` (the end-to-end test harness — it calls `kgX.ts`'s own `run*` functions directly, so it depends on both core and cli and can't live in core without core depending back on cli). Depends on `core`.",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00CDGTZHSR001",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": []
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00CDGTZHSR004",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "title": "00CDGTZHSR004",
    "text": "`packages/web` — the Solid/Vite app, stripped to a placeholder (its current content is 100% unmodified scaffold, never built out). Depends on `core`.",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00CDGTZHSR001",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": []
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00CDGTZHSR005",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
