    "title": "**A fully-dead container is never automatically cleaned up**",
    "text": "**A fully-dead container is never automatically cleaned up**: found while explaining why a service restart hadn't already collected `issues/packaging.md`'s dead nested-list-wrapper chain. Not a GC/reachability bug — `pruneUnreachableTombstones` only collects nodes that are *themselves* tombstoned and unreachable, and nothing ever tombstones a container once its last live child is gone (individual items get tombstoned one at a time as they're resolved; the now-vacuous wrapper is never itself marked dead). Promoted to [issues/core.md's Open Issues](../issues/core.md#id/BlockNode:00CF1WZ4JG006) — still belongs in a general crud/tombstone-lifecycle concern once one exists in the graph (`crud.md` is still archived, next on `archive-migration`'s own list).",
