    ],
    "title": "## Current Status",
    "text": "The restructure has landed and has been revised through v4.3 — four minor releases atop v1, a full rewrite at v2, eleven more minor releases atop that, a role split at v3, a comprehensive operational clarity rewrite at v4, and v4.1's operational gating refinements. `skills/aperas/SKILL.md` (reached by symlink from `.agents/skills/` and `.claude/skills/`) is the base every role loads, with role-specific skills defining each role's write boundaries (`aperas-orchestrator`, `aperas-grapher`, `aperas-coder`). v4 eliminated verbose prose across all skills, formalizing upfront role gating and in-flight triage. v4.1 resolved chronic gating failures by replacing passive negative prohibitions with an imperative View Triage entry bridge, establishing dual memory/rules (`.agents/rules/aperas.md`), strictly scoping native harness artifacts to human communication, and assigning codebase-tracked meta-tasks exclusively to the Coder role. The [v4](#id/BlockNode:00CTTFT4HR001), [v4.1](#id/BlockNode:00CTTFT4HR002), [v4.2](#id/BlockNode:00CVMPRD60001) and [v4.3](#id/BlockNode:00CVMPRD60002) milestones below record what each of those releases shipped, v4.2 and v4.3 being the progressive-disclosure split and the one command form with a gating drift check. Open Issues remains active, alongside the still-unmeasured [trigger accuracy against a held-out split](../planning/aperas-skill.md#id/BlockNode:00CEDFKN3000A).",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00CEA5MHD8001",
    "type": "heading",
    "children": [
      "BlockNode:00CEA5MHD8003"
    ]
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00CEA5MHD8003",
