    "title": "Defer by loading frequency once the body starts crowding",
    "text": "Defer by loading frequency once the body starts crowding: Philosophy, Orientation and Discipline stay in SKILL.md, Mechanics moves to `references/` when its bulk begins to push the levels above it out of easy reach. Not yet warranted — the body is well inside the point where deferral buys anything.",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00CFAMC7XG003",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": []
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00CEDFKN30009",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "props": [
      {
        "@id": "BlockNode:00CEDFKN30009:props:StringProp:00CFAFGDJG000",
        "@type": "StringProp",
        "key": "checked",
        "value": "true"
      }
    ],
    "title": "00CFAFGBS800B",
    "text": "Build the eval set from recorded incidents, run it against the v0 baseline preserved in git history, grade on objective assertions, and review the benchmark. This is what actually closes the Verification Plan; until it runs, the claim that the levels change behaviour is untested.",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00CFAMC7XG001",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": []
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00CEDFKN3000A",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "props": [
      {
        "@id": "BlockNode:00CEDFKN3000A:props:StringProp:00CFAFGDJG001",
        "@type": "StringProp",
        "key": "checked",
        "value": "false"
      }
    ],
    "title": "00CFAMZT8R003",
    "text": "Measure the frontmatter description against a held-out split, since triggering decides whether any of the rest is ever read. Three observations are already on record, each seen live rather than reasoned about: two sessions on an earlier, graph-edit-shaped description that loaded the skill not at all while investigating `reconcile.ts`/`node.ts`; the description that shipped as v1.3, which still did not fire; and the reordered one, which fired on turn one for a task given as \"execute AperasKG/artifacts/planning/cli.md\". None of the three was ever tried against a case it had not already been fixed against, so the held-out split is what is missing, not the labelling. The should-not-trigger class needs restating too: universal scope means nothing inside this project should fail to fire, so the negative cases are cross-project ones — sessions in repositories this graph does not cover.",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00CFAMC7XG003",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": []
  },
