    ],
    "title": "00CF9MFERG001",
    "text": "**The failed description, kept here since the commit was amended away**: the original v1.3 (`cb022b5`, reachable now only via reflog and eventually garbage-collected) opened \"Aperas is this project's external memory — a knowledge graph, worked through the `aperas` CLI, holding what has been decided, tried, found and planned, so that neither the person nor the agent has to carry it in their head. Read this at the start of any session in this project, whatever the task looks like, and before reading or changing anything. First check memory for a standing decision on whether Aperas manages the session; …\". Same instructions, same coverage, opposite order — and it did not fire. Kept here for the same reason the gate's `settings.local.json` example is: the artifact itself doesn't survive.",
