  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00CFANC9M0000",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "props": [
      {
        "@id": "BlockNode:00CFANC9M0000:props:StringProp:00CFANCBBG000",
        "@type": "StringProp",
        "key": "orderedList",
        "value": "false"
      },
      {
        "@id": "BlockNode:00CFANC9M0000:props:StringProp:00CFANCBBG001",
        "@type": "StringProp",
        "key": "startIndex",
        "value": "1"
      }
    ],
    "title": "**Batch 1 — the v1 restructure**",
    "text": "**Batch 1 — the v1 restructure**: run, but narrower than the claim. The eval set was built, run against the v0 baseline, and caught a real bug (see History). Every prompt in it exercised graph editing, though — the one path the skill already governed — so the criterion was never tried against a read-only or code-shaped task. When one finally ran against v1.3 it failed exactly where the eval had not looked: the skill loaded, was consented to, and the whole investigation still went through the projections. Verified as far as it was tested, and the test was narrower than the claim.",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00CFANC9KR001",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": []
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00CFANC9M0001",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "title": "**Deferred from Batch 1**",
    "text": "**Deferred from Batch 1**: not verified, and only one of the two is due. Deferral by loading frequency is conditional on the body crowding, which it has not. Trigger accuracy is the live one: the frontmatter description turned out to be the highest-leverage line in the file, and the version that works was reached by trial and error and confirmed at n=1 — precisely the unmeasured state its own line calls for fixing.",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00CFANC9KR001",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": []
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00CFANC9M0002",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "title": "**Batch 2 — read-side and code-side**",
    "text": "**Batch 2 — read-side and code-side**: not verified. Its criterion is behavioural and objectively checkable from a transcript, in the form the assertions paragraph above requires: given a code-shaped task in this repo, with the skill loaded and no reminder given, the first access to anything under `artifacts/` is an `aperas` call rather than `Read`/`grep`/`find`, and the session records what it found before finishing. Until that runs against a held-out prompt, Batch 2 is written-but-untested — the state Batch 1 was in before its own eval was tried.",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00CFANC9KR001",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": []
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00CFATMWY0001",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "title": "**A props-only change reports as `0 changed`, so a write that really happened is invisible in the summary**",
    "text": "**A props-only change reports as `0 changed`, so a write that really happened is invisible in the summary**: `reconcileTree`'s summary categories (matched/moved/changed/added/removed) are computed over text, so a push whose only effect is on a node's `props` — a list item's `checked`, or a run's `orderedList`/`startIndex` — comes back as `N matched, 0 changed` while a real write has occurred. Confirmed live pushing GFM checkboxes onto `planning/aperas-skill.md`'s Task Breakdown: every one of the 17 items gained a fresh `checked` StringProp and the summary reported `17 matched, 0 moved, 0 changed, 0 added, 0 removed`. Not data loss — the write lands and projects back correctly — but the summary cannot be used to confirm it, and reading it as \"nothing was written\" is the natural mistake. Same family as the skill's own \"verify by traversal, not by the summary line\", surfacing in a category the line does not cover at all. **Resolved**: `headingChanged` generalized into `pairChanged` — the existing heading text/title check, plus an order-independent `props` key/value comparison applied to *any* matched pair, not only headings. Verified live: pushing GFM checkboxes onto a scratch list now reports `0 matched, 2 changed`, and re-pushing the identical (now-checked) content afterward correctly reports `2 matched, 0 changed` — no false positives.",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00CF1WZ4JG00J",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": []
  },
