  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00CGGA9J68000",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "title": "**Root cause confirmed, and it is worse than stale titles**",
    "text": "**Root cause confirmed, and it is worse than stale titles**: `runUpdate` (`kgUpdate.ts`) only ever assigns its local `title` variable inside the `target.type === 'heading' && firstChild?.type === 'heading'` branch — for any other target (a plain paragraph/listItem), `title` stays `undefined` for the whole function, so `newShape.title = title ?? target.title` carries the *old* title forward unconditionally. It is not that the freshly-parsed title is wrong or discarded after computation — it is never read at all for a non-heading target, regardless of this session's lead-in-cap fix or anything else in `astParser.ts`.",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00CGF83D4G001",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": []
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00CGGA9J68001",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "title": "**Caught live, the expensive way**",
    "text": "**Caught live, the expensive way**: verifying that fix by re-pushing `aperas update <id>` with the node's own `--text` output (assumed to be \"the complete content,\" since `--text` is documented as the exact stored value) tombstoned 4 real nested children on `BlockNode:00CG9MDJF0001` — `--text` shows only a node's own leading text, never its children, and a non-`--text-only` `update` reconciles the piped input's (empty) overflow against the target's *real* existing children. `0 matched, 0 added, 4 removed`, not caught by the summary line alone, only by then noticing the title still hadn't updated and rechecking. Recovered via `git restore` on the staged `AperasKG/Apeiron/*.jsonld` mirror (pre-accident, from this session's own prior stage) plus `aperas reload -- --discard`; all 4 original ids verified live afterward, no data lost.",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00CGF83D4G001",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": []
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00CGGA9J68002",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "title": "00CGGA9J68002",
    "text": "This is the same shape as *Preserve identity*'s already-documented parent-heading case — an `update` reconciling children as a side effect of an operation that reads as \"just fixing the text\" — except the operator here isn't even a heading, and the tell (children present at all) is invisible from `--text` output alone. `--children` needs checking before `update` on *any* target, not only a heading.",
