    "title": "00CGJKPSD0005",
    "text": "**4. `extractAnchorNames` treats a quoted example anchor as a real claimed name** ([issues/linking.md](../issues/linking.md#id/BlockNode:00CGGHVBF8001)): fix by stripping backtick-delimited inline-code spans before running `ANCHOR_NAME_RE`, mirroring `findLeadInColonOffset`'s existing `inlineCode` exclusion (regex-based here, not AST, since every call site only ever has raw stored text). **Found while designing this fix, not yet filed as its own issue**: `stripInlineAnchors` — this session's own new storage-time call included — has the identical gap in the opposite direction: it would *strip* a legitimately backtick-quoted anchor example as if it were real projection markup, corrupting genuine prose the moment such a node is next touched (confirmed live on [`BlockNode:00CE95MVP8008`](../discussion/aperas-skill.md#id/BlockNode:00CE95MVP8008), which quotes exactly this pattern today). Both functions share `ANCHOR_NAME_RE`; fixing both from one shared \"matches outside code spans\" helper closes this before it bites, rather than after.",
