    ],
    "title": "**6. Folder-tier holders have no promotion channel** ([issues/core.md](../issues/core.md#id/BlockNode:00CF1WZ4JG009), narrowed)",
    "text": "**6. Folder-tier holders have no promotion channel** ([issues/core.md](../issues/core.md#id/BlockNode:00CF1WZ4JG009), narrowed): the issue names \"Folder/Artifact\" together, but `ArtifactNode extends BlockNode` and already passes `kg:update`'s own type check — piping any content through `kg:update` on a holder `ArtifactNode` already clears `.holder` today, confirmed by reading `kgUpdate.ts` directly. The real, narrower gap is `FolderNode` alone: `kg:insert`'s move/promote mode is hard-restricted to `BlockNode`, and `kg:update` explicitly excludes `FolderNode` from its own target-kind check, so nothing graph-first ever reaches `FolderNode.hydrateFromParsed`'s existing (and already-correct) `this.holder = undefined`. Fix: extend `kg:insert`'s anchor-*less* bare-promote branch to also accept a `FolderNode` target (reject a `FolderNode` + `--after`/`--before` combination outright, with a clear message — a folder's position comes from its path, not list order, so repositioning was never the missing piece).",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00CGK2C16G001",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": []
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00CGGTQ628003",
