    "title": "00CGJRZKJR001",
    "text": "**7. GFM task-list items leak their marker into stored text — found investigating this plan's own doubled checkboxes** ([issues/treeview.md](../issues/treeview.md#id/BlockNode:00CE1GW638007), moved up from a misdiagnosed Tier 5): `mdast-util-gfm-task-list-item` only trims the checkbox's leftover space (and re-bases the paragraph's position past it) when the item's content starts with a plain `text` node — bold, italic, inline code, and link lead-ins all leave the marker in, since CommonMark's inline tokenizer never materializes that lone leading space as its own text node. Fix: `astParser.ts` defensively strips a leading `[ ]`/`[x]` from both `.text` and `.title` for any listItem already known to be a checkbox. Verified end-to-end, then applied to fix this very plan's own six checkboxes, which had rendered doubled (`[ ] [x]`) before it.",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00CGK2C16G001",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": []
