  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00CGM4YD4G001",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "tombstonedAt": "2026-09-15T08:34:02.896Z",
    "title": "**`aperas update` re-derives an `ArtifactNode` target's own title from pushed text, corrupting its file-basename identity and breaking its own path resolution**",
    "text": "**`aperas update` re-derives an `ArtifactNode` target's own title from pushed text, corrupting its file-basename identity and breaking its own path resolution**: found while updating this doc's own leading-summary text (every concern doc's `ArtifactNode.text` carries a short current-status headline as a graph-side-only field, never projected into the actual `.md` file) — `issues/core.md`'s `ArtifactNode` itself had its `title` silently overwritten with a re-derived lead-in term from whatever text was last pushed to it, instead of staying `\"core.md\"` (the file basename `trackFromDisk` sets once at track time). Confirmed by direct inspection: the corruption already existed in the last committed state, predating this session's own work. Broke `aperas unfold issues/core.md`/every other bare-path resolution of that artifact outright — `findChild`'s slug match is title-based, uniformly for every tree-positioned kind, so a wrong title makes the artifact unreachable by its own path even though its `path` field and structural position were both still correct. **Root cause**: `kgUpdate.ts`'s non-heading title re-derivation (`if (target.type !== 'heading') { title = firstChild.title; }`, added by an earlier fix in this same session for the equivalent, correct bug on ordinary blocks — see [item 1](#id/BlockNode:00CF1WZ4JG003)) never excluded `ArtifactNode` targets, even though an `ArtifactNode`'s title is never a function of its own text the way a block's lead-in is. **Resolved**: the condition now also checks `kind !== 'ArtifactNode'`, leaving `title` `undefined` (and so `target.title` unchanged) whenever the update target is an artifact root. `issues/core.md`'s own title was manually corrected back to `\"core.md\"`; two other artifacts found with the same stale-but-otherwise-harmless symptom (`issues/treeview.md`'s own leading summary describing an issue already resolved) were refreshed to `\"None.\"` while confirming the title fix held. Verified live: re-pushing `issues/documentation.md`'s own \"None.\" text through the fixed code left its title untouched.",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00CF1WZ4JG00J",
    "type": "paragraph",
    "children": []
  },
