          }
        ]
      }
    ],
    "title": "## Links breaking twice this session, via unrelated mechanisms — the substrate itself is fragile in ways nothing detects",
    "text": "Follows directly from [the earlier finding that `kg:update`/`kg:insert` never resolved wikilinks at all](../discussion/linking.md#id/BlockNode:00CF1276D0001) — that was fixed, and a graph-wide sweep found and fixed 9 real cases of the resulting staleness. Two things surfaced today, in the same session, that mean the fix wasn't the end of the story:",
    "type": "heading",
    "children": [
      "BlockNode:00CGMX2YZG002",
      "BlockNode:00CGMX2YZG003",
      "BlockNode:00CGMX2YZR000"
    ]
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00CGMX2YZG002",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "title": "00CGMX2YZG002",
    "text": "A fresh corpus-wide check (not the original sweep's own scope) found the identical symptom already back on nodes the original sweep never had reason to touch — `planning/core.md`'s own Batch 1 item 1 (`BlockNode:00CGGTQ620002`) has an empty `.links` despite an unchanged real citation in its text, and it was never part of the original 9. The sweep fixed a snapshot; nothing keeps re-checking it, so drift just accumulates again under a different name.",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00CGMX2YZG001",
    "type": "paragraph",
    "children": []
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00CGMX2YZG003",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "title": "Separately and more concerning",
    "text": "Separately and more concerning: four nodes each had a link genuinely resolve during today's own work — `aperas update --text-only` reported \"N resolved\" for every one — and each still ended up with an empty `.links` afterward, caught only because a reader (not a check) asked to look at one directly. Reproducing it under controlled conditions failed every way tried: matching move-then-update sequences (single and 4-node batches), a sibling heading's plain reconcile in between, a full service restart, and the exact stop → manual JSON edit → start sequence used elsewhere in this same session for an unrelated fix. Re-running the same unchanged `update --text-only` a second time did resolve and this time persist correctly.",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00CGMX2YZG001",
    "type": "paragraph",
    "children": []
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00CGMX2YZR000",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "links": [
      {
        "@id": "BlockNode:00CGMX2YZR000:links:Link:00CGMX3248000",
        "@type": "Link",
        "target": "BlockNode:00CGMWQ6T0001",
        "predicate": "[[wikilink]]",
        "props": [
          {
            "@id": "BlockNode:00CGMX2YZR000:links:Link:00CGMX3248000:props:StringProp:00CGMX3248001",
            "@type": "StringProp",
            "key": "position",
            "value": "12"
          }
        ]
      }
    ],
    "title": "00CGMX2YZR000",
    "text": "Promoted to [issues/linking.md's Open Issues](../issues/linking.md#id/BlockNode:00CGMWQ6T0001) — filed as one open item covering both, since they share the same consequence (a claim's provenance silently gone with nothing to notice) even though their causes are unrelated and the second one's cause isn't known yet.",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00CGMX2YZG001",
    "type": "paragraph",
    "children": []
  },
