            "@type": "StringProp",
            "key": "position",
            "value": "12"
          }
        ]
      }
    ],
    "title": "### Mechanics — the view-cleanup gap is closed",
    "text": "Supersedes: [v2's own \"nothing prunes a view's unfolds\" line](#id/BlockNode:00CGF613W8016)",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00CGN8W9M8001",
    "type": "heading",
    "children": [
      "BlockNode:00CGN8W9MG006"
    ]
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00CGN8W9MG006",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "title": "00CGNAHPQR001",
    "text": "Cheapest discipline is a named view per task rather than one long-lived default — creating one is a single call, and a view scoped to the task documents its own contents. `unfold` now refuses a ref with no quads at all at write time, and an explicit sweep (`aperas reload`, service shutdown) strips any `unfolds` entry that's gone stale since — but a tombstoned-yet-present target is left alone by both, since it's a legitimate, revealable-via-`--tombstoned` entry, not a stale one.",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00CGN8W9MG005",
    "type": "paragraph",
    "children": []
  },
