    ],
    "title": "00CJ2WQ1SR001",
    "text": "**A third instance, 2026-09-17, with a new and much broader trigger.** Creating [discussion/webapp.md](../discussion/webapp.md#id/BlockNode:00CJ2TCV40001) ended with three `aperas update --text-only` calls whose only purpose was promoting the holder flags off the ArtifactNode, the H1 and the `## Dashboard` heading — writes that changed no text at all and touched no link-bearing block. `aperas check-links` immediately afterwards reported **8** discrepancies across the artifact, every one of them on list items several levels below the promoted headings, none of which was the target of any of the three writes. Each had reported its links resolved correctly when it was first inserted, and `aperas show` had confirmed the stored `Link` objects on three of them before the promotions ran. What makes this instance different from the two above is the blast radius: the damage was not confined to the node written, or even to its own subtree edited — a no-op text write at the top of a document dropped `.links` from unrelated descendants elsewhere in it. `check-links --repair` restored all 8 in one pass. Promoted to [issues/linking.md's Open Issues](../issues/linking.md#id/BlockNode:00CJ38Z8T0001).",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00CGMX88R0001",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": []
