    "children": []
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00CJ3A5850002",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "tombstonedAt": "2026-09-17T15:34:24.432Z",
    "title": "**Graph-wide sweep for the pre-fix \"wikilink never resolved\" residue — 9 real cases found and fixed, not the 20 first estimated**",
    "text": "**Graph-wide sweep for the pre-fix \"wikilink never resolved\" residue — 9 real cases found and fixed, not the 20 first estimated**: `resolveBlockLinks` used to run only from `kg:ingest`, never `kg:update`/`kg:insest` ([this doc's own account above](#id/BlockNode:00CF1276D0001)) — already fixed in the current code, but every node last touched before that fix kept a permanently-empty `.links` regardless of what its text actually cited. A first pass (any stored `text` containing `](...#...)`with an empty `.links`) found 20 candidates graph-wide; most turned out to be false positives once checked by hand — a fenced code-block example in `design/documentation.md` with placeholder ids (`00C0000000001`, all zeros), and half a dozen copies of `SKILL.md`'s own wikilink-syntax documentation quoting the pattern with a literal `<ID>`/`...` placeholder inside backticks, none of them real citations at all. Re-run comparing each node's *actual* `#id/BlockNode:...` fragments (code fences and inline-code spans excluded from the count) against its resolved `.links` targets found exactly 9 genuine cases, spread across `planning/linking.md`, `issues/packaging.md`, `history/aperas-skill.md` and `discussion/aperas-skill.md` — all resolvable (every target confirmed live, none tombstoned or missing). Fixed by re-touching each with `aperas update <id> --text-only` (piping the node's own unchanged text) — chosen over a plain `update` specifically because a plain reconcile risks tombstoning real children on a node whose full shape isn't known up front (the near-miss recorded just above this entry); `--text-only` never reconciles children at all, so it was safe regardless. Confirmed by re-running the same precise sweep afterward: zero remaining. A companion check for the opposite failure — a resolved `Link` whose *target* is now dead or missing — also came back empty, so this concern's link integrity is otherwise clean as of this pass.",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00CGGG6N5G001",
    "type": "paragraph",
    "children": []
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00CJ3A5N48001",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "tombstonedAt": "2026-09-17T15:34:14.715Z",
    "title": "00CJ3A5N48001",
    "text": "> tsx packages/cli/src/aperas.ts show BlockNode:00CGFE4SV0002 --text",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00CGFE4SV0002",
    "type": "blockquote",
    "children": []
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00CJ3A5N48002",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "tombstonedAt": "2026-09-17T15:34:15.574Z",
    "title": "**`aperas update` never re-derives a non-heading block's title**",
    "text": "**`aperas update` never re-derives a non-heading block's title**: replacing a paragraph's `.text` leaves `.title` frozen at whatever ingest originally derived from the lead-in term, even when the new text no longer has that lead-in at all — so the block goes on previewing under a title for content it no longer holds. Root cause confirmed directly in `kgUpdate.ts`: `runUpdate`'s local `title` variable is assigned only in the heading-target/heading-input branch — for a paragraph/listItem target it stays `undefined` for the entire function, so the old title is carried forward unconditionally, every time, not merely left stale by a parsing quirk. Also confirmed worse than a stale-title problem: verifying it by re-pushing a node's own `--text` output (assumed complete) tombstoned that node's 4 real children, since `--text` never shows children and a non-`--text-only` update reconciles the piped (empty) overflow against what's really there. Recovered via the staged `git` checkpoint; see [discussion/linking.md](../discussion/linking.md#id/BlockNode:00CGGA9J68000) for the full incident. Invisible in the rendered projection, since only a heading's title is ever written back to disk (`kg:title`'s removal made the lead-in term the one and only title mechanism, with `update` compensating for heading targets only) — but `tree`, `unfold` and `backlinks --text` all display the stale title in the graph itself, with the summary line's `0 changed` giving no hint either way. No CLI route yet to repair an already-stale title short of tombstoning the block. Found live while rewriting `design/aperas-skill.md`'s Topology paragraph for the `aperas` skill's v2; full account in [discussion/linking.md](../discussion/linking.md#id/BlockNode:00CGF83D4G001). **Resolved**: `runUpdate`'s paragraph branch now reads `title = firstChild.title` too (already computed by the parser for every paragraph, nothing new to derive), skipped only when `target` itself is a heading (where `firstChild` is the adopted leading paragraph, a different piece of text from the heading's own title). Decoupled from `props`, which must stay untouched for a non-heading re-title — a new `retitling` flag (true only for an actual heading retitle) now gates the two prop-replacement sites that used to key off `title !== undefined` alone. Verified live: a scratch paragraph's title updates on content change and a scratch listItem's `orderedList`/`startIndex`/`checked` props survive a title-changing update untouched; a real heading retitle still replaces its own props (tree-anchor) as before.",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00CGFE4SV0002",
    "type": "paragraph",
    "children": []
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00CJ3A6178001",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "tombstonedAt": "2026-09-17T15:34:26.879Z",
    "title": "00CJ3A6178001",
    "text": "> tsx packages/cli/src/aperas.ts show BlockNode:00CDBYV5A800K --text",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00CDBYV5A800K",
