  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00CJ3A6178002",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "tombstonedAt": "2026-09-17T15:34:27.650Z",
    "title": "**Collision check only covered a block's current slug-path**",
    "text": "**Collision check only covered a block's current slug-path**: resolved — Slice 2's collision check (`apeironNgn/node.ts`'s `rejectSlugPathCollisions`) checks every anchor `name` still embedded in a block's `treeAnchor` prop or raw text too, not just its current `toPath()`, since [Anchor-Matching Requirement for Resolution](../design/linking.md#id/BlockNode:00CDBYV4TG005) already treats either as a live resolvable target. See [Planning](../planning/linking.md#id/BlockNode:00CDBZ77F000X).",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00CDBYV5A800K",
    "type": "paragraph",
    "children": []
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00CJ3A6CZ0001",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "tombstonedAt": "2026-09-17T15:34:28.563Z",
    "title": "00CJ3A6CZ0001",
    "text": "> tsx packages/cli/src/aperas.ts show BlockNode:00CDBYV5A800J --text",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00CDBYV5A800J",
    "type": "blockquote",
    "children": []
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00CJ3A6CZ0002",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "tombstonedAt": "2026-09-17T15:34:29.309Z",
    "title": "**A lead-in colon followed only by nested list children got no title**",
    "text": "**A lead-in colon followed only by nested list children got no title**: resolved — `findLeadInColonOffset`'s space-after-colon check read the next character from the colon's own mdast text node, which simply ends at the colon when nothing inline follows it on the same line (e.g. `- **Heading**:` before a nested list), and treated that the same as a genuinely ambiguous no-space case. Fixed by accepting \"nothing left in this text run\" the same as \"a space follows\" — the inline-code and bold/italic exclusions run first and are unaffected. See [Lead-In Term Detection](../design/linking.md#id/BlockNode:00CDBYV4TG000) and [Discussion](../discussion/linking.md#id/BlockNode:00CDBZ76TR00E).",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00CDBYV5A800J",
    "type": "paragraph",
    "children": []
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00CJ3A6T88001",
