  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00CJ3A6T88002",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "tombstonedAt": "2026-09-17T15:34:25.982Z",
    "title": "**Cross-artifact link staleness on ingestion**",
    "text": "**Cross-artifact link staleness on ingestion**: resolved — an artifact whose own text doesn't change is never re-ingested on its own, so a link it couldn't resolve stayed stale even after its target came into existence elsewhere in the corpus, with no way to fix it short of hand-editing `ingestedHash` to force a re-ingest. `kg:ingest` now stashes every code a block fails to resolve on its own referring artifact, and retries every stashed code against the current graph after its main work is done, force-reingesting (without discarding reconciliation identity — see [Discussion](../discussion/linking.md#id/BlockNode:00CDBZ76TR008) for the `hadContent`/`bypassUnchangedCheck` distinction) any artifact where at least one now resolves. See [Workflows](../design/linking.md#id/BlockNode:00CDBYV4TG007).",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00CDBYV5A800H",
    "type": "paragraph",
    "children": []
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00CJ3A7610001",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "tombstonedAt": "2026-09-17T15:34:33.462Z",
    "title": "00CJ3A7610001",
    "text": "> tsx packages/cli/src/aperas.ts show BlockNode:00CDBYV5A800G --text",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00CDBYV5A800G",
    "type": "blockquote",
    "children": []
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00CJ3A7610002",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "tombstonedAt": "2026-09-17T15:34:34.195Z",
    "title": "00CJ3A7610002",
    "text": "**Every `<block-slug-path>` written so far omitted its own H1 segment.** `toPath()` (`apeironNgn/node.ts:455-471`) walks every `BlockNode` ancestor — the H1 heading included — contributing a slug segment for each, stopping only at the owning `ArtifactNode`/`FolderNode`. Every anchor and cross-reference in this concern's own docs had been computed without that leading segment (traced back to the very first `test-slugifed-path.md` validation, which never included its own H1 either) and has been corrected corpus-wide. See [Topology](../design/linking.md#id/BlockNode:00CDBYV4T8007).",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00CDBYV5A800G",
    "type": "paragraph",
    "children": []
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00CJ3A7JDR001",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "tombstonedAt": "2026-09-17T15:34:35.122Z",
    "title": "00CJ3A7JDR001",
    "text": "> tsx packages/cli/src/aperas.ts show BlockNode:00CDBYV5A800F --text",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00CDBYV5A800F",
    "type": "blockquote",
    "children": []
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00CJ3A7JDR002",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "tombstonedAt": "2026-09-17T15:34:35.864Z",
    "title": "**\"Duplicate-slug collisions\"**",
    "text": "**\"Duplicate-slug collisions\"**: misdiagnosed — a collision only happens when two blocks share an identical *full* slug-path (same heading text at the exact same tree position), a genuine authoring error, correctly a hard reject, not a case needing disambiguation logic. Reusing the same heading title at different tree positions is ordinary and never collides, since the full path includes the distinguishing ancestor segments. See [Topology](../design/linking.md#id/BlockNode:00CDBYV4T8007).",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00CDBYV5A800F",
    "type": "paragraph",
    "children": []
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00CJ3A810G001",
