        "@type": "StringProp",
        "key": "startIndex",
        "value": "1"
      }
    ],
    "title": "00CJ3Q48PR000",
    "text": "**Fixed, verified, and the earlier account above overstated `kg:update`'s own safety.** `collectOldWikilinksByBlock` gained a `recursive` parameter (default `true`, preserving every existing caller); `repairLinkIntegrity` now calls it once per named discrepant block with `recursive: false`, so `oldWikilinksByBlock`'s key population can never exceed `pendingLinks`' own — the exact invariant the bug violated. `verify:slow`'s step 19 fixture gained a second, unrelated citation pair in the same artifact specifically to catch a regression of this: its `Link` id is asserted unchanged after a repair of the *other*, deliberately-dropped citation, which fails against the old code and passes against the fix. Both `verify` and `verify:slow` pass in full.",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00CGMX88R0001",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": []
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00CJ3Q48PR001",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "links": [
      {
        "@id": "BlockNode:00CJ3Q48PR001:links:Link:00CJ3Q4B2R002",
        "@type": "Link",
        "target": "BlockNode:00CJ38Z8T0001",
        "predicate": "[[wikilink]]",
        "props": [
          {
            "@id": "BlockNode:00CJ3Q48PR001:links:Link:00CJ3Q4B2R002:props:StringProp:00CJ3Q4B30000",
            "@type": "StringProp",
            "key": "position",
            "value": "815"
          }
        ]
      }
    ],
    "title": "Correcting the earlier claim that `kg:update --text-only`'s own `collectOldWikilinksByBlock(target, ...)` call \"scopes correctly\"",
    "text": "Correcting the earlier claim that `kg:update --text-only`'s own `collectOldWikilinksByBlock(target, ...)` call \"scopes correctly\": it does not, in general — it recurses into `target`'s existing children by default, exactly like the pre-fix `repairLinkIntegrity` did over a whole artifact. The 16-block restore above only avoided the bug because every target was a *leaf* (no children to recurse into): `oldWikilinksByBlock` came back empty regardless, so the union with `codesByBlock` added nothing extra. The *same* mechanism, on a target that does have real children, is exactly what dropped `.links` from `00CGN6GJV8002`/`00CJ38Z8T0001` (editing their parent `00CGMWQ6T0001`) and then again from those same two nodes (editing `00CDBYV5A8002` moments later) — both confirmed live, both recovered the same way, in [issues/linking.md's Open Issues (3)](../issues/linking.md#id/BlockNode:00CJ38Z8T0001)'s own account. This is very likely item (3)'s actual root cause, not merely a related instance of it: every one of item (3)'s original three holder-promotion writes was itself an `update --text-only` on a heading with real, untouched children. `kg:update --text-only` is not yet fixed — the natural next fix, using the same `recursive: false` parameter, would call `collectOldWikilinksByBlock(target, oldWikilinksByBlock, false)` and instead build old-wikilink entries for the piped `overflow` blocks separately (they're new content, not `target`'s existing children, so nothing to collect old links for) — not yet implemented, pending a decision to proceed.",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00CGMX88R0001",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": []
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00CJ3Z5DM0001",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "links": [
      {
        "@id": "BlockNode:00CJ3Z5DM0001:links:Link:00CN1KQQZR000",
        "@type": "Link",
        "target": "BlockNode:00CGMWQ6T0001",
        "predicate": "[[wikilink]]",
        "props": [
          {
            "@id": "BlockNode:00CJ3Z5DM0001:links:Link:00CN1KQQZR000:props:StringProp:00CN1KQQZR001",
            "@type": "StringProp",
