      }
    ],
    "title": "**Resolved**",
    "text": "**Resolved**: root cause was a scope mismatch shared with `check-links --repair`'s own bug above — `kg:update --text-only`'s `collectOldWikilinksByBlock(target, ...)` recursed into `target`'s *existing* children by default, while its own `pendingLinks` covers only `target` itself plus the freshly piped `overflow`. `resolveBlockLinks`'s key-union then reprocessed every untouched existing child with zero pending codes, wiping its real `.links`. Fixed the same way: `collectOldWikilinksByBlock` gained a `recursive` flag, and `kg:update` now passes `recursive: false` specifically for `--text-only` (the reconcile branch stays recursive, correctly, since its `pendingLinks` already covers the whole subtree). `verify:slow` gained a dedicated step (20) with a parent-plus-real-child fixture, asserting the child's `Link` id survives a `--text-only` update to the parent untouched — confirmed to fail against the pre-fix code and pass against the fix. Verified live against the actual corpus too: re-running the exact `--text-only` update on [`BlockNode:00CGMWQ6T0001`](../issues/linking.md#id/BlockNode:00CGMWQ6T0001) that triggered this twice during (1)/(3)'s own write-up left both children's `Link` ids completely unchanged, with no integrity warning. Full account in [discussion/linking.md](../discussion/linking.md#id/BlockNode:00CJ2WQ1SR001).",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00CJ38Z8T0001",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": []
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00CJ4H44J8001",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "props": [
      {
        "@id": "BlockNode:00CJ4H44J8001:props:StringProp:00CJ4H4718000",
        "@type": "StringProp",
        "key": "orderedList",
        "value": "false"
      },
      {
        "@id": "BlockNode:00CJ4H44J8001:props:StringProp:00CJ4H4718001",
