    "title": "**Resolved: bare-path corpus links (no `#id/...` fragment) rendered inert in the UI**",
    "text": "**Resolved: bare-path corpus links (no `#id/...` fragment) rendered inert in the UI**: `design/linking.md`'s Context section links `**Discussion**`/`**Planning**` by plain relative path with no fragment at all — a form the graph's own resolver never even attempted to resolve until the same-day core fix (see [History](../history/linking.md#id/BlockNode:00CJAVGNJG001)). Resolving it in the graph wasn't enough on its own: `Inline.tsx` has no server round trip of its own to learn a link's target, so it still needs a `#id/<Kind>:<id>` fragment sitting in the href text itself. Fixed with `bakeResolvedLinkIds` (`apeironNgn/node.ts`), which bakes each already-resolved bare-path link's target into its href for the render tree only — the stored text and every projected file stay untouched. Verified live in a real browser: clicking both links now navigates to their target `ArtifactNode`, breadcrumbs and content updating correctly.",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00CJ6V637000F",
