  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00CJDHHVA8000",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "title": "**Until the tick channel ships, a client-side poll stands in**",
    "text": "**Until the tick channel ships, a client-side poll stands in**: the dev tab bumps its own refetch every 1s regardless of whether anything actually changed, through the same refetch path an in-page fold/edit action already uses — so an external `aperas fold`/`unfold`/CLI write is picked up without a manual reload. User-toggleable (a `sync` checkbox in the header), since a poll racing a session that's deliberately mid-edit via the CLI is more noise than help. Deliberately not the design above: it's a poll, not a push, and it lives entirely client-side rather than in the service.",
