    ],
    "title": "**`kg:unfold` never got the breadcrumb `kg:tree` did**",
    "text": "**`kg:unfold` never got the breadcrumb `kg:tree` did**: [the fix above](#id/BlockNode:00CJ01QAJ0000) only touched `kgTree.ts` — `kg:unfold`'s own output (`kgUnfold.ts`) kept printing straight from `id  [label]  title`, no `aperas://tree/<path>` anywhere, even though its own target is exactly as reusable a `<ref>` as a tree render's apex is. **Resolved**: same format, same placement — one line before the target's own, computed the same way (`TreeNode.toPath()`), omitted rather than printed broken wherever `toPath()` can't walk it. For the `Link` case, the breadcrumb names the *target*'s path, not the Link's own (a Link has none — same reason the ref resolver can't route one through path-segment matching either), matching the target getting the full/uncapped text treatment right below it.",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00CE1GW63800A",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": []
  },
