    "title": "**Ctrl-click on the fold arrow folds instead of zooming, and swallows the event**",
    "text": "**Ctrl-click on the fold arrow folds instead of zooming, and swallows the event**: `FolderDiv.tsx`'s `Gutter` is the only click site in that file which never checks `ctrlKey`/`metaKey` — the node line, both link-row modes and the backlinks popover all do — and because its handler calls `e.stopPropagation()`, the row's own zoom handler never sees the event either. So ctrl-clicking the arrow silently folds and the zoom is simply lost, which reads as \"zoom doesn't work\" to anyone who aims at the control rather than at the title; found by a user hitting it on first use of the app. This contradicts the settled design rather than filling a gap in it: [zoom in is a new apex](../discussion/webapp.md#id/BlockNode:00CJ2V1YAR009) specifies the gesture on the arrow itself (\"ctrl-clicking a fold arrow re-renders with that node as apex\"), so the implementation has never matched what was agreed. Fixing it is also a precondition for [the redesigned gesture set](../discussion/webapp.md#id/BlockNode:00CMWMP6X8001), where ctrl must work uniformly on the row, the arrow and the stem.",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00CJ6V6370002",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": []
  },
