    "title": "**Resolved: every block-structured node rendered as one flattened run of literal markup in the UI — tables and fenced code were unreadable**",
    "text": "**Resolved: every block-structured node rendered as one flattened run of literal markup in the UI — tables and fenced code were unreadable**: a `[table]` showed as `| a | b | | --- | --- | | 1 | 2 |` in flowing prose, and a `[code]` block showed its own ``` fences as text with every line rewrapped, destroying column alignment. Two causes, both fixed: every `RenderNodeItem.abstract` is a one-line preview with all whitespace collapsed (`truncateForPreview`, `astParser.ts`), and `Inline.tsx` was deliberately inline-only with no block-level renderer at all. [AnDT1211's `feat/web-markdown-rendering`](../history/webapp.md#id/BlockNode:00CPYRTRA0001) added real block-level renderers (`MarkdownTable.tsx`, `CodeBlock.tsx`) that read a node's own full `.text` instead of the collapsed `.abstract`. Verified live against this exact corpus's own [fold/unfold redesign](../discussion/webapp.md#id/BlockNode:00CMWMP6X8001) content, the issue's original worked example: a real 6-row `<table>` and a code block with preserved line breaks and alignment, confirmed via direct DOM inspection. A third cause originally filed here — the row's own title falling back to a raw snowflake id — has no clear fix yet and isn't the same shape of problem, so it's split out as [its own open issue](#id/BlockNode:00CQ0KYYQG000).",
