    "title": "**A node's fold state is two axes: whether it is pinned, and how much of its children shows**",
    "text": "**A node's fold state is two axes: whether it is pinned, and how much of its children shows**: `unfolds` membership is the first axis; a per-node *level* — stashed, titles, previews — is the second, and applies only to a pinned node. The two together produce six states, plus a seventh (cut off by `maxDepth`) that belongs to the render rather than to the node and so carries no arrow at all — there the `…` marker is itself the control. One shape, two fills, three angles: `▶` (U+25B6) pinned, `▷` (U+25B7) not, rotated 0°/45°/90° through the `transform` transition `.fd-arrow` already carries. Angle reads east-nothing, southeast-partially, south-fully, so `▷` never reaches south: an unpinned node never shows children as content. `●` (U+25CF, not the too-small U+2022) marks a pinned leaf, a confirmed dead end. [Every state tabulated, and why two axes rather than one bit](../discussion/webapp.md#id/BlockNode:00CMWKJYR0001).",
