            "@type": "StringProp",
            "key": "position",
            "value": "803"
          }
        ]
      }
    ],
    "title": "**The stem is the fold control; a passive guide marks path**",
    "text": "**The stem is the fold control; a passive guide marks path**: a solid, hoverable stem appears only where a node is pinned *and* its children render as content, so clicking it always folds and never promises an action that isn't there. A row showing a child only because something deeper is pinned — a breadcrumb — gets a non-interactive sparse dotted guide instead (`repeating-linear-gradient`, roughly 2px on / 5px off; `╎` on the console), which is what tells a path stairway apart from real content. This restores the rule the [arrow and its stem are one control](#id/BlockNode:00CJDHYES8001) already implied and the Solid port lost by keying the stem on \"has children\". On the console the prefix has to be built from a per-level stack rather than `'│ '.repeat(depth)`, which cannot vary per column. [Rationale](../discussion/webapp.md#id/BlockNode:00CMWMMRGG001).",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00CJ6TGSYR000",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": []
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00CMX5G968001",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "links": [
      {
        "@id": "BlockNode:00CMX5G968001:links:Link:00CMX5GBM0000",
        "@type": "Link",
        "target": "BlockNode:00CMWMVMV0001",
        "predicate": "[[wikilink]]",
        "props": [
          {
            "@id": "BlockNode:00CMX5G968001:links:Link:00CMX5GBM0000:props:StringProp:00CMX5GBM0001",
            "@type": "StringProp",
            "key": "position",
            "value": "469"
          }
        ]
      }
    ],
    "title": "**The webapp's depth limit is derived from available width**",
    "text": "**The webapp's depth limit is derived from available width**: `floor((width − buffer) / gutter)` against a fixed `1.2rem` gutter, recomputed and refetched (debounced) on resize, and kept as `maxDepth` on the server render rather than truncated client-side so that `truncated` keeps a single meaning. A legibility backstop rather than a performance cap — at a typical viewport it lands far past anything this corpus nests to, so the `…` control is rare by construction. [Rationale](../discussion/webapp.md#id/BlockNode:00CMWMVMV0001).",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00CJ6TGSYR000",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": []
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00CMX5GNB0001",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "links": [
      {
        "@id": "BlockNode:00CMX5GNB0001:links:Link:00CMX5GQQ0000",
        "@type": "Link",
        "target": "BlockNode:00CMWMRX88001",
        "predicate": "[[wikilink]]",
        "props": [
          {
            "@id": "BlockNode:00CMX5GNB0001:links:Link:00CMX5GQQ0000:props:StringProp:00CMX5GQQ0001",
            "@type": "StringProp",
            "key": "position",
            "value": "539"
          }
        ]
      }
    ],
    "title": "**`TreeView` carries the child-display level as two orthogonal subset fields**",
    "text": "**`TreeView` carries the child-display level as two orthogonal subset fields**: `unfolds` keeps membership alone, so every existing sweep over it is untouched; `unfoldsCollapsed` and `unfoldsNoPreview` are subsets of it, and the default level (previews) is the absence of both, costing no storage. Orthogonal rather than one ordered scalar so that no mutual-exclusion invariant has to be enforced in code, and so that stashing remembers the level to return to. Both new fields have to join `removeDanglingUnfolds` and `pruneStaleUnfolds`. [The four sub-states, and why not a reified entry](../discussion/webapp.md#id/BlockNode:00CMWMRX88001).",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00CJ6TGSYG005",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": []
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00CMXB0X6R001",
