  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00CN0MVG2R001",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "title": "**(4) A third scope-mismatch site: `ArtifactNode.ingestFromDisk`'s tombstone-holdback branch, on `aperas ingest --track` (not `kg:update`)**",
    "text": "**(4) A third scope-mismatch site: `ArtifactNode.ingestFromDisk`'s tombstone-holdback branch, on `aperas ingest --track` (not `kg:update`)**: found live while testing the new frontmatter-`description` feature on `design/treeview.md` — adding frontmatter to an already-tracked artifact whose reconcile also happened to find an unrelated, pre-existing pending removal (a stale tombstoned `list` node left over from the list-consumption migration, held back since `--force` wasn't passed) silently wiped `.links` on 6 of that same artifact's own Context-section bullets (`**Discussion**`/`**Issues**`/`**Planning**`/`**History**`), none of them touched by the frontmatter edit at all. Same root-cause class as (3), a different call site: `ingestFromDisk`'s early return (tombstones pending, `!force`) hands back `pendingLinks: descriptionPendingLinks` only — the full-body `extractLinkCodes(finalRoot)` never runs, since that happens after this return point — but `oldWikilinksByBlock`/`oldLinkTargets` were collected recursively over the *whole* artifact before the tombstone gate ran. `resolveBlockLinks`'s key-union then reprocessed every other block with zero pending codes and wiped its real `.links`, exactly the invariant `collectOldWikilinksByBlock`'s own doc comment warns against. Repaired live via `aperas check-links --repair` (6 → 0 discrepancies).",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00CGMWQ6T0001",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": [
      "BlockNode:00CN0MYWT0001"
    ]
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00CN0MYWT0001",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "title": "**Resolved**",
    "text": "**Resolved**: fixed at the actual early-return site (`node.ts`'s `ArtifactNode.ingestFromDisk`) — `oldLinkTargets`/`oldWikilinksByBlock` are now trimmed down to just the artifact's own key before being returned, instead of handing back the full-artifact maps, matching the same scoping (3)'s fix already established for `kg:update --text-only`/`repairLinkIntegrity`. New regression test: `verifyExtended.ts` step 22 (a citing block with a real resolved link, plus a sibling paragraph removed between two ingests specifically to trip the tombstone-confirmation gate without `--force`) — confirmed to fail against the pre-fix code and pass against the fix. `npm run verify` and `npm run verify:slow` both pass clean end to end against the fixed corpus.",
