    "title": "00CN8KC5W8002",
    "text": "Both items were written when Orientation had no subsections at all, and were silently re-scoped the moment \"Deep read and deep write run along the same three directions\" was introduced above them: in a flat layout a paragraph belongs to whatever heading precedes it, so an item written for the section level is captured by the first subsection that appears before it, with nothing marking which one it was meant for. Neither item lost or gained a word — each bold lead-in simply became the `###` heading it had been acting as. Promotion rather than relocation is what restores the scoping, since once a subsection opens there is no way back to section level except to precede every subsection or to carry a heading of one's own.",
