  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00CNR1X7RG001",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "tombstonedAt": "2026-09-23T07:32:20.182Z",
    "title": "**The webapp's 1s poll causes a full-tree remount, not a genuine reload, 2026-09-23**",
    "text": "**The webapp's 1s poll causes a full-tree remount, not a genuine reload, 2026-09-23**: `App.tsx`'s `refreshTick` signal drives `createResource`'s key (`{apex, view, tick}`), so every poll fetches a brand-new `TreeResponse` — a fresh object graph with new references top to bottom, even when nothing changed. `FolderDiv.tsx`'s recursive `<For each={n.children}>` reconciles by object reference, not by id, so it cannot match old items to new ones: it tears down and remounts every row in the tree every second, dropping any open inline editor (`editing` signal) mid-edit and resetting scroll/focus. Fix is `reconcile(data, {key: 'id'})` from `solid-js/store`, merging each poll's response into a persistent store keyed by node id instead of handing `<For>` a fresh object graph each time — recorded as its own pattern in the `solidjs` skill's *Reconciling polled/re-fetched data into a store* section.",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00CJ2TESY0003",
    "type": "paragraph",
    "children": []
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00CNR1X7RG002",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "tombstonedAt": "2026-09-23T07:32:21.525Z",
    "title": "Reconciling by a single `id` key surfaced a second, unrelated defect",
    "text": "Reconciling by a single `id` key surfaced a second, unrelated defect: `RenderLinkItem` (`core/src/apeironNgn/node.ts`) names its identifier `linkId`, unlike every other `RenderItem` variant and unlike the graph itself — `BlockNode.jsonld`'s `@id` is a single uniform field across every node kind, links included. Traced to [Proposed shape of the structured render](#id/BlockNode:00CJ2VBQR0003), which introduced the split with no stated rationale. Renamed to `id` across `RenderLinkItem`, `buildLinkItem`'s construction sites, `toText`'s link branch, and the webapp's mirrored type and consumers, so `reconcile` keys uniformly across both `RenderItem` variants and the naming matches the corpus's own convention.",
