    ],
    "title": "**`resolveEffectiveGraphName()` resolved from the wrong process's cwd, 2026-09-23**",
    "text": "**`resolveEffectiveGraphName()` resolved from the wrong process's cwd, 2026-09-23**: undetected until Slices 2/3/16 were verified against a genuine second graph, since this repo's own dev setup always runs the service with `cwd: monorepoRoot` (`vite.config.ts`'s spawn), where the ancestor-walk-then-fallback happened to land on AperasKG either way. The production listener calls `resolveEffectiveGraphName()` with no `startDir` from *inside* the long-lived service process — whose cwd, for a packaged binary, is wherever it's installed, never the graph's directory. Confirmed live: `aperas serve` from a throwaway graph's own directory reported `{\"name\":\"AperasKG\"}` over `/api/graph` while genuinely serving the throwaway graph's tree content. Fixed by giving name resolution the same `APERAS_GRAPH_NAME` env-var passthrough `APERAS_APEIRON_ROOT`/`APERAS_ARTIFACTS_ROOT` already had — resolved once, correctly, by `bindAndSpawn` (`kgService.ts`) from *its own* cwd (the same place the other two roots are resolved from) and threaded through `spawnService` into the child's env. The doc comment this session wrote for `resolveEffectiveGraphName` when the graph-name feature first landed claimed \"No env-var override... nothing to pass between a spawning and a spawned process\" — wrong, corrected in place rather than left to mislead the next reader. Folded into [Resolved: Slice 16 — packaging](../issues/webapp.md#id/BlockNode:00CNSME9ZG000).",
