            "key": "position",
            "value": "496"
          }
        ]
      }
    ],
    "title": "**2026-09-25: single `~` no longer strikes through**",
    "text": "**2026-09-25: single `~` no longer strikes through**: GFM's default `singleTilde: true` turned `range 5~10 and 20~30` into \"5<del>10 and 20</del>30\" (hit in real use). The shared processor in `markdown.ts` now passes `remarkGfm` `{ singleTilde: false }`, so only `~~x~~` strikes and a single `~` (approximately, ranges, `~/` paths) renders literally. A corpus-wide parse beforehand found no existing strikethrough of either form, so nothing depended on the single-tilde form. Web-only, alongside [inline/display math](#id/BlockNode:00CQ2N1Z1R000): `core` uses `remark-gfm` only for block boundaries, which strikethrough never affects.",
