    ],
    "title": "**v3 — the skill split across three agents, communicating through views, because one agent can no longer follow the whole loop**",
    "text": "**v3 — the skill split across three agents, communicating through views, because one agent can no longer follow the whole loop**: on 2026-09-27 the workflow has grown past what a single agent follows reliably — the user routinely has to remind agents (Claude, and Antigravity more so) of the steps they dropped. Proposed: an orchestrator that talks with the user, a grapher that owns the graph, a coder that owns the code, with the graph itself as the interface — a view tracks the state of the work (data), chat tracks its progress (control). Settled in the same conversation, promoted to [Multi-agent working](../design/aperas-skill.md#id/BlockNode:00CR3X3N00001) and planned as [Batch 3](../planning/aperas-skill.md#id/BlockNode:00CR3XQKNG001):",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00CE8XWZK0001",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": [
      "BlockNode:00CR3XZ220002",
      "BlockNode:00CR3XZ228000",
      "BlockNode:00CR3XZ228001",
      "BlockNode:00CR3XZ228002",
      "BlockNode:00CR3XZ228003",
      "BlockNode:00CR3XZ228004",
      "BlockNode:00CR3YAK1R001",
      "BlockNode:00CR4MZMD8001",
      "BlockNode:00CR541P8R001",
      "BlockNode:00CR3XZ228005"
    ]
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00CR3XZ220002",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "props": [
      {
        "@id": "BlockNode:00CR3XZ220002:props:StringProp:00CR3XZ4YG000",
        "@type": "StringProp",
        "key": "orderedList",
        "value": "false"
      },
      {
        "@id": "BlockNode:00CR3XZ220002:props:StringProp:00CR3XZ4YG001",
        "@type": "StringProp",
        "key": "startIndex",
        "value": "1"
      }
    ],
    "title": "**Write scope**",
    "text": "**Write scope**: the orchestrator writes only freeflow recording the chat and its own turns in subagent threads; coder writes only its thread; grapher does everything else — deep read, deep write, every promotion, thread lifecycle.",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00CR3XZ220001",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": []
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00CR3XZ228000",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "title": "**Loop, not three steps**",
    "text": "**Loop, not three steps**: first proposed as grapher → coder → grapher, corrected to an open-ended alternation, grapher always first — coder's first phase is usually a survey, which grapher files before any code changes.",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00CR3XZ220001",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": []
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00CR3XZ228001",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "title": "**Messages keep their arguments**",
    "text": "**Messages keep their arguments**: an early restatement reduced every hand-off message to \"the view is updated, your turn\"; rejected — a view is `this`, and a call still needs its other arguments. Folding everything into one view is possible in principle and unnatural in practice.",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00CR3XZ220001",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": []
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00CR3XZ228002",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "title": "**Scale**",
    "text": "**Scale**: `concepts` was first placed below `discussion`, then corrected above it — design > {issues, planning, history} > concepts > discussion > thread. Threads being lowest is what forbids anything outside them from linking in.",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00CR3XZ220001",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": []
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00CR3XZ228003",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "title": "**Views gain a root**",
    "text": "**Views gain a root**: long on the user's wait list; only the current root is recorded, and each turn creates a new root node over mostly-reused content rather than rewriting the view's contents.",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00CR3XZ220001",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": []
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00CR3XZ228004",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "title": "**Threads**",
    "text": "**Threads**: stored in `.state/` by subtree membership, an option chosen over introducing new node kinds so every verb keeps working unchanged; pruning is ordinary tombstoning, triggered by a size-cap warning on every thread write.",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00CR3XZ220001",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": []
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00CR3XZ228005",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "title": "**Platforms**",
    "text": "**Platforms**: Antigravity confirmed to support markdown agent definitions with preloaded skills (`.agents/agents/<name>.md`, `subagent: true`, `skills:`), matching Claude Code's `.claude/agents/`.",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00CR3XZ220001",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": []
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00CR3YAK1R001",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "title": "**Subturns carry tool results, not only narration**",
    "text": "**Subturns carry tool results, not only narration**: first described as running progress-and-reasoning notes; corrected to also hold the essence of each tool result a later turn will need — written as it happens or at the end of the turn, but always written, since a later turn has only the thread to recover it from.",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00CR3XZ220001",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": []
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00CR4MZMD8001",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "title": "**Asking back is a first-class duty, on par with subturns**",
    "text": "**Asking back is a first-class duty, on par with subturns**: in the first skill draft it sat inside the coder's \"no turn without a Report\" rule; separated out, because it is what distinguishes these subagents from an ordinary one, which runs to completion and returns its best guess at the gaps.",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00CR3XZ220001",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": []
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00CR541P8R001",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "title": "**`Every claim carries its source` generalized to every role, not copied wholesale into the grapher skill**",
    "text": "**`Every claim carries its source` generalized to every role, not copied wholesale into the grapher skill**: the first draft copied v2.11's whole section into `aperas-grapher`, since only the grapher writes formal docs; corrected, because the underlying rule — a claim needs traceable provenance wherever it is written — is Philosophy's evidence rule and binds freeflow and thread entries too, not only formal-doc ones. Split: the general principle moved to the base skill's Discipline, the formal-doc-specific origin-placement mechanics stayed in `aperas-grapher` as `Provenance at the origin`, citing the base rule it applies.",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00CR3XZ220001",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": []
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00CR5AWY6R001",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "title": "# Concepts",
    "text": "Shared vocabulary and relationships surfaced across concerns and threads, promoted up by the grapher once they recur across tasks.",
    "parent": "ArtifactNode:00CR5AEJ88000",
    "type": "heading",
    "children": []
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00CR5GCSEG001",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "links": [
      {
        "@id": "BlockNode:00CR5GCSEG001:links:Link:00CR5GCWWR000",
        "@type": "Link",
