    "title": "## v3.1 additions — delta on the v3 snapshot",
    "text": "Threaded onto [the v3 snapshot](#id/BlockNode:00CR5GCSEG001), across all four skill files. Implements [Skill v3.1 — decisions from the first-run findings](#id/BlockNode:00CR81Y470001), which answer the defects [the first live run of the v3 loop](#id/BlockNode:00CR7N7Z60001) surfaced: the orchestrator's staging exemption contradicting its own section, no guidance for a discussion without `## Freeflow`, the orchestrator surveying for itself, a grapher Ask that folded in the coder's survey, and freeflow lagging the conversation. The full task loop moves into the base skill so every role sees the turns around its own; the orchestrator's *Running a task* now follows it step for step, and each role skill's survey is scoped to its own side. Written by the orchestrator in the skill files and recorded here afterwards by the grapher, as the decision itself directed.\nTwo entries were added the same day under [the follow-up decisions](#id/BlockNode:00CR8G0T70001): subturns required in *Threads*, and the drift-script path corrected in the grapher skill. A further entry, [the skill asks for detailed records](#id/BlockNode:00CR98HFCG001), added tool-gap recording and filing across all four skill files. [Fixing the misleading \"if you include them\" clause](#id/BlockNode:00CR9KFCN0001) corrected two bullets in the base skill's *Updating an existing list item*. Two more followed: [threads may link to each other](#id/BlockNode:00CRAX4MZ0001) reworded the thread-tier rule in the base and grapher skills, and [the pre-send checklist for Asks](#id/BlockNode:00CRAX4MZ8000) added a new section to the orchestrator skill.",
