    "title": "**Decided — correct the drift-script path**",
    "text": "**Decided — correct the drift-script path**: `aperas-grapher/SKILL.md` names `scripts/skill_drift.py`, but the script lives at `skills/aperas/scripts/skill_drift.py` (repo root has no `scripts/`). The orchestrator fixes the skill text; the grapher records it.",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00CR8G0T70001",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": []
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00CR8G0T78000",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "title": "**Decided — history milestones**",
    "text": "**Decided — history milestones**: the grapher adds v3 and v3.1 milestones to `history/aperas-skill.md`, whose milestones stop at v2.",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00CR8G0T70001",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": []
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00CR8G0T78001",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "title": "**Decided — fix the heading level of the later version sections**",
    "text": "**Decided — fix the heading level of the later version sections**: in `discussion/aperas-skill.md`, the v2.3 deltas onward (through the v3 snapshot and the v3.1 delta) sit at the document root instead of under the H1 like v0–v2.2. The user noticed this long ago and left it. The grapher fixes it by moving the nodes, keeping their ids.",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00CR8G0T70001",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": []
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00CR8G0T78002",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "title": "**Decided — subturns are required, not optional as a level**",
    "text": "**Decided — subturns are required, not optional as a level**: the user questioned the base skill's *Threads* wording \"Subturns are optional as a level and mandatory as content\", and approved the fix 2026-09-27. The Work line holds the approach in one line and subturns hold results, so no multi-call turn can fold them in, and a single-call turn's result is already in the Report. The rule becomes: at least one subturn per batch of tool calls, each holding that batch's results. The orchestrator edits the skill; the grapher records it.",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00CR8G0T70001",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": []
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00CR8G1CP8001",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "title": "**The webapp opens a newly loaded view at the folder root, not at the view's root**",
    "text": "**The webapp opens a newly loaded view at the folder root, not at the view's root**: reported by the user 2026-09-27. A view's root is its current zoom (set by `aperas zoom`), which is also where `aperas tree --view` renders from by default. The webapp should open a view there too.",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00CJ2TESY0003",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": []
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00CR8JD5VG001",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
