    ],
    "title": "### aperas — Discipline — Threads, every turn has subturns",
    "text": "Supersedes: [v3's subturn paragraph in Threads](#id/BlockNode:00CR5GCSF000K)",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00CR874TC8001",
    "type": "heading",
    "children": [
      "BlockNode:00CR8JD5VG002"
    ]
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00CR8JD5VG002",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "title": "00CR8JD5VG002",
    "text": "**Every turn has subturns: at least one per batch of tool calls.** The Work line holds the approach in one line; the results belong in subturns, and no turn with more than one call can fold them into that line. For each batch, a subturn records the progress, the reasoning, and the *essence of each tool result* a later turn will need — the failing assertion's line, the id that came back, the count, the file that turned out to own the behavior — not \"ran the tests\". Write them as you go or at the end of the turn, but before the turn ends: a result that is not in the thread is gone for every later turn, since the next invocation starts from the thread, not from this one's context.",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00CR8JD5VG001",
    "type": "paragraph",
    "children": []
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00CR8JDSQG001",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
