    "title": "**v3.1 — the first live run of the loop failed on the skill's own defects, and the full task loop moved into the base**",
    "text": "**v3.1 — the first live run of the loop failed on the skill's own defects, and the full task loop moved into the base**: the first task run under v3, the same day, was reset as a failed try before any code was written. The orchestrator's staging exemption contradicted its own section, a topic discussion without `## Freeflow` left it with no guidance, it surveyed the corpus itself, and its first Ask folded the coder's survey into the grapher's turn; freeflow lagged the conversation throughout. The fix put the whole turn sequence — grapher survey, coder survey, grapher files, coder change, orchestrator verifies, grapher files — into the base skill, so every role sees the turns around its own ([The loop](../design/aperas-skill.md#id/BlockNode:00CR3X3N08001)). Every role now stages its own writes, every Ask cites the freeflow nodes for the decisions it relies on, and the orchestrator reads for itself only by recording what it relays. Two follow-ups the same day made subturns required, at least one per batch of tool calls ([threads](../design/aperas-skill.md#id/BlockNode:00CR3X3N08004)), and corrected the drift-script path. The three tool issues the run found were held back as v3.1's test tasks. Recorded as [the v3.1 delta](../discussion/aperas-skill.md#id/BlockNode:00CR874TC8001). Notable as the first version written under the split v3 introduced: the orchestrator edited the skill files and the grapher recorded them.",
