    "title": "**v2.1 — link-write verification named as the sharpest instance of \"verify by traversal\"**",
    "text": "**v2.1 — link-write verification named as the sharpest instance of \"verify by traversal\"**: two confirmed-live incidents in one session — a corpus-wide sweep finding 9 nodes whose links had silently never resolved, and a separate incident watching four freshly-resolved links vanish from nodes that had just been moved and re-texted — showed a write can report `\"N resolved\"` and still leave `.links` empty, with nothing else surfacing it. Discipline's \"Verify by traversal\" item was rewritten to treat a link-bearing write as unverified until `aperas show`/`aperas backlinks --text` actually shows the `Link`. Recorded as [the v2.1 delta](../discussion/aperas-skill.md#id/BlockNode:00CGMY04AG001).",
