    "title": "**v2.5 — `check-links` moved from a discipline to remember into a check the service runs itself**",
    "text": "**v2.5 — `check-links` moved from a discipline to remember into a check the service runs itself**: documenting the tool in v2.4 without attaching discipline to it left it exactly where Philosophy warns against — available, correct, and dependent on somebody remembering to run it. Two of the three checks moved into the service (per-write and corpus-wide-at-reload sweeps); only the end-of-batch sweep remains an agent's own responsibility. Measured before designing: a corpus-wide sweep costs about 0.6s, so \"too expensive to run often\" — the premise the first design cut rested on — was false. Recorded as [the v2.5 delta](../discussion/aperas-skill.md#id/BlockNode:00CHYJ6PR8001).",
