    "title": "**v2.10 — `aperas update` generalized to adopt a parsed node's full state, closing the checkbox gap v2.3 left open**",
    "text": "**v2.10 — `aperas update` generalized to adopt a parsed node's full state, closing the checkbox gap v2.3 left open**: found while updating `planning/webapp.md`'s checkboxes — piping `- [x] ...` at an existing item nested it exactly as v2.3's warning predicted, but unlike plain text there was no bare-paragraph escape hatch, since checkbox state can only be expressed through the marker itself. Verifying the fix surfaced two more defects closed in the same change: a title-rederivation bug adopting a throwaway parse-time id instead of leaving the old title alone, and a spurious-run-leader hazard from naively adopting a solo item's ordering props. `aperas insert`'s ordered-list append picked up a matching fix, validating the number it is given instead of silently discarding it. Recorded as [the v2.10 delta](../discussion/aperas-skill.md#id/BlockNode:00CNW4V5GG001).",
