    "title": "**v2.8 — reading gained a direction rule of its own, confirmed once each way in one session**",
    "text": "**v2.8 — reading gained a direction rule of its own, confirmed once each way in one session**: the concern gradient that already governs where a citation may point was found to also govern where a read may enter, with drift between a tier and what it governs visible only where a top-down descent and a bottom-up pinpoint meet. One confirmation per direction: a code-entry fix that worked while leaving its design clause stale, and a top-down read that quoted a design rule its own projection had replaced thirteen versions earlier. Settled as [Entry route](../design/aperas-skill.md#id/BlockNode:00CN7XM9TG001); two paragraphs were relocated, not rewritten, to fix a dangling \"both\" the new subsection had orphaned. Recorded as [the v2.8 delta](../discussion/aperas-skill.md#id/BlockNode:00CN7YEND0001).",
