    "title": "**A stdin-less `aperas insert --after` (a move) hung in the grapher's shell, cause unknown**",
    "text": "**A stdin-less `aperas insert --after` (a move) hung in the grapher's shell, cause unknown**: found 2026-09-27. The grapher stopped the call, reran it with `< /dev/null`, and it succeeded. The orchestrator first blamed `readStdinIfPiped` in `packages/cli/src/kgInsert.ts` (it reads stdin to end-of-file whenever stdin isn't a TTY). But in the orchestrator's shell stdin is `/dev/null` and reaches end-of-file at once, so that read cannot block there. Unconfirmed alternatives: the subagent's shell has a different stdin, or the service was unresponsive (it dropped or was slow to start twice the same session) and the retry simply came later. Related but distinct: [the unscoped `aperas ingest` hang on a confirmation prompt](../issues/core.md#id/BlockNode:00CNX1T4XG001).",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00CR81TAV8001",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": []
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00CR92W8TR001",
