    "title": "**Friction — a text-only `aperas update` on a list item tombstones its children**",
    "text": "**Friction — a text-only `aperas update` on a list item tombstones its children**: the orchestrator piped only the item's own text (from `aperas show --text`) to fix a lead-in, and the item's two children were tombstoned (`BlockNode:00CR98J7KR002`, `BlockNode:00CR98J7KR003`, since recreated). The base skill's *Updating an existing list item* says that leaving the text out clears it. It does not say that leaving the children out removes them, and \"this also updates any nested children in the same call, if you include them\" reads as if omitted children are left alone.",
