    "title": "**Decided — fix the misleading \"if you include them\" clause**",
    "text": "**Decided — fix the misleading \"if you include them\" clause**: User, 2026-09-27. [the update-tombstones-children friction](../discussion/aperas-skill.md#id/BlockNode:00CR994X80001) read as if omitting children left them alone; the CLI's own `--help` and the actual behavior say otherwise. Fixed in the base skill's *Updating an existing list item*: the text-change bullet now says a bare-text update replaces children too, and the text-clears bullet is rewritten as one symmetric rule — whichever side (text or children) you don't restate is wiped. The orchestrator edits the skill; the grapher records it.",
