    "title": "00CR9P6W40002",
    "text": "**For an ordinary text change, pipe bare text with no bullet marker** (e.g. `updated text`, not `- updated text`). This replaces the item's children too, not just its text — see the last point below for what that costs if you don't restate them. See the next point for the cases that need a marker instead.",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00CR9P6W40001",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": []
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00CR9P6W40003",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "title": "00CR9P6W40003",
    "text": "**The rule runs both ways: whichever piece you don't restate is wiped, not left alone.** Piping only new children (a list, with no text of its own before it) clears the item's own text — unlike the title, nothing here is left alone by default. Piping only text with no children after it tombstones any existing children the same way, since the call reconciles them against what was piped, which was none. Confirmed live: fixing a lead-in term by piping the item's corrected text alone, with no children, cost it two children that had to be reinserted. Restate whichever side you're not touching.",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00CR9P6W40001",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": []
  },
