    "title": "**Report**",
    "text": "**Report**: every truncation point in `tree`'s and `unfold`'s preview paths is mapped, with what depends on each and what doesn't — the coder's own survey can start from this rather than re-deriving it.",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": []
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00CR9Y09Y0001",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "title": "00CR9Y09Y0001",
    "text": "**Orchestrator verified the coder's Turn 1 survey** (the coder's Turn 1 Report in `.threads/coder.md`): `packages/web/src/Inline.tsx:106-107`'s link-hover popover reads `node.abstract` with no fallback — confirmed by reading the file, matching the coder's caution against uncapping at the render-tree source. `packages/web/src/FolderDiv.tsx:342,553,609` each already write `n.text ?? n.abstract` (or `l().text ?? l().abstract`) — confirmed, so the print-side fallback is a precedented pattern already live in the webapp, not a new one. `kgUnfold.ts`'s `previewChildren` (lines 102-117) does call the capped `previewText` per child/link, matching the coder's additional finding beyond the Ask's literal scope.",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00CE1DDF58003",
