      }
    ],
    "title": "**The fix**",
    "text": "**The fix**: `toText()` in `packages/core/src/apeironNgn/node.ts` picks the capped `item.abstract` over the already-present uncapped `item.text` at two print sites — `:1943` for node rows, `:1956` for link rows. Swapping to `item.text ?? item.abstract` at both is the entire change; `buildNodeItem`/`buildLinkItem` (`:1813`/`:1874`) keep computing `abstract` exactly as today. Promoted to [design/treeview.md's Rendering section](../design/treeview.md#id/BlockNode:00CRA8JPFR001).",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00CR9ZBSB0001",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": []
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00CR9ZBSB0003",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "title": "**Why print-side, not source-side**",
    "text": "**Why print-side, not source-side**: `packages/web/src/Inline.tsx:106-107`'s link-hover popover reads `node.abstract` directly with no fallback, deliberately wanting a short preview in a tooltip. Uncapping `abstract`'s computation inside `buildNodeItem`/`buildLinkItem` would silently uncap that popover too. The print-side fallback is also not a new pattern: `packages/web/src/FolderDiv.tsx:342,553,609` already write `n.text ?? n.abstract` (or `l().text ?? l().abstract`) for the same `RenderItem` shape.",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00CR9ZBSB0001",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": []
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00CR9ZBSB0004",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "title": "**Nothing else reads `abstract`**",
    "text": "**Nothing else reads `abstract`**: `hiddenCount` comes from `treeChildren.length`/`links.length` deltas, `truncated` from `opts.maxDepth` vs `depth`, and the `[+N]` fold tag reads `hiddenCount` — all three are depth/count mechanisms independent of text length.",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00CR9ZBSB0001",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": []
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00CR9ZBSB0005",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "title": "**Beyond the Ask's literal scope**",
    "text": "**Beyond the Ask's literal scope**: `kgUnfold.ts`'s `previewChildren()` (lines 102-117) still calls `previewText()` with no `{full: true}` for every child/link preview line, even though the unfolded target's own top line already passes `{full: true}` (lines 155/161). `kgBacklinks.ts:43` calls the identical non-full branch of `nodeAbstract()` — the same mechanism, not a separate cap.",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00CR9ZBSB0001",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": []
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00CR9ZBSB0006",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "title": "00CR9ZBSB0006",
    "text": "**Scope resolved**, from the user's own wording (\"remove all output length cap (tree & unfold)\"): the print-side fix in `toText()` is in scope; `kgUnfold.ts`'s `previewChildren` loses its cap too, since it's part of unfold's own output; `kgBacklinks.ts` stays capped, since the user named `tree`/`unfold` and not `backlinks`, and an uncapped backlinks list multiplies output in a way a single `tree`/`unfold` reveal doesn't.",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00CR9ZBSB0001",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": []
  },
  {
