      }
    ],
    "title": "**Decided — threads may link to each other** (user, 2026-09-27)",
    "text": "**Decided — threads may link to each other** (user, 2026-09-27): threads sit on the same tier, so a link between them is sideways and allowed. A coder Ask citing the grapher's Report is fine. What stays forbidden is any link into a thread from outside the threads tier: formal docs, `concepts.md`, discussion. The base skill's \"nothing outside a thread links into one\" is reworded to say so.",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00CRAQQ2V0001",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": [
      "BlockNode:00CRAZZ8A0001"
    ]
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00CRAX4MZ8000",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "title": "**Decided — apply the pre-send checklist for Asks** (user, 2026-09-27)",
    "text": "**Decided — apply the pre-send checklist for Asks** (user, 2026-09-27): the orchestrator skill gains a checklist to run on every Ask before dispatch: only the receiver's kind of work, a freeflow citation for every decision, cite rather than retype, one task per dispatch. The user also noted that the run's rule failures — surveying the code three times and retyping content across Asks — explain why it took much longer than the old single-agent workflow.",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00CRAQQ2V0001",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": [
      "BlockNode:00CRAZZWR0001"
    ]
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00CRAZ91C8001",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "links": [
      {
        "@id": "BlockNode:00CRAZ91C8001:links:Link:00CRAZ95M8000",
