    "title": "**Cap removal only reaches one level down, not a whole subtree**",
    "text": "**Cap removal only reaches one level down, not a whole subtree**: verified live 2026-09-27, after the cap-removal fix landed. Genuinely unfolding a node now auto-reveals full, uncapped text for its *direct* children (the tier-2 preview), which is a real improvement — a single Work or Report node's subturns now read in one `unfold` + `tree --view`. But grandchildren stay fully collapsed behind a bare `[+N]` count, revealing nothing, confirmed against a real 3-level chain in `design/linking.md`. A genuinely deep, cross-cutting read — several Turns' chains plus separate entries elsewhere — still needs a script or many manual unfolds, one per level, same as before the fix.",
