  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00CRBYWS98002",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "title": "00CRBYWS98002",
    "text": "```markdown\n# Grapher thread\n## <topic>                                   ← named by the user\n### <task>                                   ← set by the orchestrator\n#### Turn <n>                                ← one exchange with the orchestrator\n- **Ask**: <what is wanted, in a sentence>   ← orchestrator; root of <p>-orchestrator-grapher\n  - [<argument>](../design/x.md#id/BlockNode:…) — why it matters here\n- **Work**: <the approach, in a line>        ← subagent; subturns nested under it\n  - <subturn>\n- **Report**: <the outcome, in a sentence>   ← subagent; root of <p>-grapher-orchestrator\n  - [<changed or found node>](…) — what changed, or what it shows\n  - **Question**: <whatever the Ask left unsettled — see below>\n  - **Tool gap — <what>**: <a workaround built, a call that failed or hung — see below>\n  - **Tool gap — <what else>**: <a second one, if the turn hit more than one>\n```",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00CRBYWS98001",
    "type": "code",
    "children": []
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00CRBYWS98003",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "title": "00CRBYWS98003",
    "text": "More than one **Tool gap** in a Report needs a distinct lead-in for each — `<what>`, not a bare repeat of the word \"Tool gap\" — since sibling slugs are derived from the lead-in term, and two identical ones collide outright: the write is rejected in full, nothing written, before either one lands.",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00CRBYWS98001",
    "type": "paragraph",
    "children": []
  },
