  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00CTVWQ9G0001",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "title": "**Decision — promote and fix subagent tool gap and correct Orientation order (2026-10-01)**",
    "text": "**Decision — promote and fix subagent tool gap and correct Orientation order (2026-10-01)**: User confirmed that subagent harness tool gap is a blocking issue that must be promoted to the graph and resolved immediately. Technical approach combines in-session runtime subagent definitions (`define_subagent` with `enable_write_tools: true`) to equip active subagents with file-writing and CLI execution tools, with persistent updates to `.agents/agents/*.md` for future sessions. Instead of a synthetic smoke test, `aperas-coder` executes real work: placing `Mandatory Initial Gate` first under `## 2. Orientation` in `skills/aperas/SKILL.md` with an imperative bridge pointing to View Triage, followed by `View Triage & Management`, `Entering the Corpus`, and `Three Traversal Directions`.",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00CE8XWZK0001",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": []
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00CTVZR8P0001",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "links": [
      {
        "@id": "BlockNode:00CTVZR8P0001:links:Link:00CTVZREW0000",
