      }
    ],
    "title": "**Sparse CLI `--help` and lack of AST piping recipes**",
    "text": "**Sparse CLI `--help` and lack of AST piping recipes**: Neither `aperas insert --help` nor `aperas update --help` explains how piped markdown trees are parsed into node kinds, how list-item parentage works, or when child nodes are preserved vs. reconciled. The skill runbooks instruct agents to \"write subturns and Report\" into threads, but provide no canonical CLI recipes (e.g. `cat << 'EOF' | aperas insert <parent> --after <sibling>`).",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00CTX70TQ0001",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": []
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00CTX70TQ0003",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "title": "**Subagents reading engine source code (`kgInsert.ts` & `kgUpdate.ts`)**",
    "text": "**Subagents reading engine source code (`kgInsert.ts` & `kgUpdate.ts`)**: Facing sparse help and knowing that Aperas's reconciler can silently drop or scramble child nodes if used incorrectly on list items (a known failure mode documented in `discussion/aperas-skill.md`), both subagents refused to guess. Grapher read lines 1–190 of `kgInsert.ts` and searched `kgUpdate.ts`. Coder, after applying its 16-second code edit, spent ~4.5 minutes reading 260 lines of `kgInsert.ts` and all 458 lines of `kgUpdate.ts` to verify the exact behavior of `--text-only` and child reconciliation before updating its Report node.",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00CTX70TQ0001",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": []
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00CTX70TQ0004",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "title": "**Interactive overwrite prompt hang in `aperas project` (Step 111)**",
    "text": "**Interactive overwrite prompt hang in `aperas project` (Step 111)**: `aperas project` halted on an unhandled interactive prompt (`Overwrite ...? (yes/no)`) when target projected files had local uncommitted modifications. Running in a non-interactive subagent shell, the process hung in the background. Grapher lost ~45 seconds detecting the stall, yielding, and manually feeding `yes\\n` via `manage_task send_input`, later learning to pipe `echo yes | aperas project`.",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00CTX70TQ0001",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": []
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00CTY63E98001",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "props": [
      {
