        "key": "orderedList",
        "value": "false"
      },
      {
        "@id": "BlockNode:00CTY63E98002:props:StringProp:00CTY63M40001",
        "@type": "StringProp",
        "key": "startIndex",
        "value": "1"
      }
    ],
    "title": "**Removal of Table of Contents in v4 rewrite**",
    "text": "**Removal of Table of Contents in v4 rewrite**: In earlier versions of `SKILL.md`, a Table of Contents gave agents an immediate roadmap of the file within the first 50 lines. The v4 rewrite dropped the TOC, starting directly with Philosophy and Orientation. Because subagents do not see the document's structure up front, they cannot know that Section 4 (*Mechanics*) exists further down.",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00CTY63E98001",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": []
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00CTY63E9G000",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "title": "**Agent-initiated slice truncation**",
    "text": "**Agent-initiated slice truncation**: The `view_file` tool supports up to 800 lines and 46 KB per call, easily accommodating `SKILL.md` (422 lines, 24.5 KB) in full. However, subagents self-limited: Grapher explicitly requested `StartLine: 1 EndLine: 100`, while Coder requested `StartLine: 1 EndLine: 250`. Neither agent issued follow-up reads for the remainder of the file. Without a TOC or explicit section pointers, agents assumed the top 100–200 lines were complete and never loaded Section 4's list-handling rules into context.",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00CTY63E98001",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": []
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00CTY63E9G001",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "title": "**Incomplete & misleading command references (`--after` omission and list-item `--text-only` vacuum)**",
    "text": "**Incomplete & misleading command references (`--after` omission and list-item `--text-only` vacuum)**: Line 219 (`Insert Turn Node`) documented `cat ask.md | aperas insert <turn-id>`, omitting `--after <ask-id>` and failing to explain how multi-block Work + Report trees are parsed, which drove Coder to read `kgInsert.ts`. Line 222 and line 309 warned that updating a list item replaces its children, while lines 221 and 320 documented `--text-only` strictly for headings. Fearing that updating its Report node would tombstone its 4 subturn children, Coder read all 458 lines of `kgUpdate.ts` to verify that `req.textOnly` works on `listItem` targets.",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00CTY63E98001",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": []
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00CTY63E9G002",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "title": "**Proposed solutions across base and role skills**",
    "text": "**Proposed solutions across base and role skills**: Concrete structural remedies to eliminate subagent CLI hesitation and source-code reads:",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00CTX70TPR001",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": [
      "BlockNode:00CTY63E9G003",
      "BlockNode:00CTY63E9G004",
      "BlockNode:00CTY63E9G005",
      "BlockNode:00CTY63E9G006"
    ]
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00CTY63E9G003",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "props": [
      {
        "@id": "BlockNode:00CTY63E9G003:props:StringProp:00CTY63M40002",
