        "key": "orderedList",
        "value": "false"
      },
      {
        "@id": "BlockNode:00CTY63E9G003:props:StringProp:00CTY63M40003",
        "@type": "StringProp",
        "key": "startIndex",
        "value": "1"
      }
    ],
    "title": "**Restore Table of Contents with stable heading anchors in base `skills/aperas/SKILL.md`**",
    "text": "**Restore Table of Contents with stable heading anchors in base `skills/aperas/SKILL.md`**: Add a concise Table of Contents right after the preamble, mapping the 5 core sections (`## 1. Philosophy`, `## 2. Orientation`, `## 3. Discipline`, `## 4. Mechanics`, `## 5. Reference`) using stable section heading anchors. Avoid hardcoded line numbers which drift across edits; subagents can grep for line numbers if specific tool view ranges are needed.",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00CTY63E9G002",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": []
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00CTY63E9G004",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "title": "**Complete CLI reference in base `SKILL.md`**",
    "text": "**Complete CLI reference in base `SKILL.md`**: Update `Insert Turn Node` to include `--after <anchor>` and explain multi-node tree piping; update `Updating an Existing List Item` to explicitly document `echo \"updated text\" | aperas update <id> --text-only --flush` for preserving child blocks.",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00CTY63E9G002",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": []
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00CTY63E9G005",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "title": "**Self-contained turn recipes in role skills**",
    "text": "**Self-contained turn recipes in role skills**: Add ready-to-run turn insertion snippets (`cat << 'EOF' | npm run aperas -- insert <turn-id> --after <ask-id> --flush`) directly into `skills/aperas-coder/SKILL.md` and `skills/aperas-grapher/SKILL.md`.",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00CTY63E9G002",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": []
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00CTY63E9G006",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "title": "**Explicit navigation pointers in role skills**",
    "text": "**Explicit navigation pointers in role skills**: Add explicit pointers in role skills guiding subagents to Section 4 (*Mechanics*) of the base skill whenever they need syntax details beyond their turn recipe.",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00CTY63E9G002",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": []
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00CTYF5W48001",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "title": "**Subagent dispatch mechanism — stateless per-turn invocation across harnesses (Antigravity `invoke_subagent` vs Claude Code `Task`) (2026-10-01)**",
    "text": "**Subagent dispatch mechanism — stateless per-turn invocation across harnesses (Antigravity `invoke_subagent` vs Claude Code `Task`) (2026-10-01)**: Trajectory and architectural analysis establishing that subagent turns must always be dispatched as fresh, stateless invocations rather than stateful conversational continuations:",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00CE8XWZK0001",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": [
      "BlockNode:00CTYF5W48002",
      "BlockNode:00CTYF5W48003",
      "BlockNode:00CTYF5W48004",
      "BlockNode:00CTYF5W48005"
    ]
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00CTYF5W48002",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "props": [
      {
        "@id": "BlockNode:00CTYF5W48002:props:StringProp:00CTYF61A8000",
        "@type": "StringProp",
        "key": "orderedList",
        "value": "false"
      },
      {
        "@id": "BlockNode:00CTYF5W48002:props:StringProp:00CTYF61A8001",
        "@type": "StringProp",
        "key": "startIndex",
        "value": "1"
      }
    ],
    "title": "**Incident — Grapher Turn 2 transcript bloat (220 steps, 278 KB)**",
    "text": "**Incident — Grapher Turn 2 transcript bloat (220 steps, 278 KB)**: In Turn 2 of `### promote-and-fix-subagent-tool-gap`, Orchestrator dispatched Grapher via `send_message` targeting its Turn 1 conversation ID (`97ddc9af`). This appended Turn 2 into Turn 1's history rather than resetting context. By the end of Turn 2, Grapher's transcript reached 220 steps and ~278 KB, dragging along Turn 1's Apeiron service restart attempts, interactive prompt stalls, and 50-line JSON-LD grep dumps.",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00CTYF5W48001",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": []
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00CTYF5W48003",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "title": "**Root cause — Antigravity built-in continuation heuristic vs Aperas memory model**",
    "text": "**Root cause — Antigravity built-in continuation heuristic vs Aperas memory model**: Antigravity's generic harness prompt advises agents to send follow-up messages to existing subagents to \"conserve resources\" for natural continuations. This advice directly contradicts Aperas's core architectural principle: **The Apeiron graph and `.threads/{role}.md` are the working memory, not the LLM's conversation history.** Reusing subagents causes context rot, token bloat, and degrades multi-turn reasoning.",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00CTYF5W48001",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": []
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00CTYF5W48004",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "title": "**Harness compatibility comparison — Claude Code `Task` vs Antigravity `invoke_subagent`**",
    "text": "**Harness compatibility comparison — Claude Code `Task` vs Antigravity `invoke_subagent`**: In Claude Code, subagent delegation via the `Task` tool is inherently ephemeral and stateless: each `Task` invocation is a fresh instance with zero prior session history (Claude Code has no `send_message` equivalent). Antigravity supports both `invoke_subagent` (stateless fresh spawn) and `send_message` (stateful continuation). Mandating `invoke_subagent` per turn in Antigravity unifies behavior with Claude Code's native execution model.",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00CTYF5W48001",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": []
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00CTYF5W48005",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "title": "**Orchestrator skill guidance & harness-agnostic wording**",
    "text": "**Orchestrator skill guidance & harness-agnostic wording**: `skills/aperas-orchestrator/SKILL.md` must explicitly mandate stateless per-turn dispatch using universal discipline paired with harness tool mappings:",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00CTYF5W48001",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": [
      "BlockNode:00CTYF5W48006",
      "BlockNode:00CTYF5W48007",
      "BlockNode:00CTYF5W48008"
    ]
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00CTYF5W48006",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "props": [
      {
        "@id": "BlockNode:00CTYF5W48006:props:StringProp:00CTYF61AG000",
        "@type": "StringProp",
        "key": "orderedList",
        "value": "false"
      },
      {
        "@id": "BlockNode:00CTYF5W48006:props:StringProp:00CTYF61AG001",
        "@type": "StringProp",
        "key": "startIndex",
        "value": "1"
      }
    ],
    "title": "*Universal rule*",
    "text": "*Universal rule*: Always dispatch a fresh subagent instance for every turn; subagents in Aperas are stateless workers. Never carry conversation history across turns.",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00CTYF5W48005",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": []
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00CTYF5W48007",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "title": "*Tool mappings*",
    "text": "*Tool mappings*: In Antigravity, call `invoke_subagent` (never `send_message` across distinct turns); in Claude Code, call `Task`.",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00CTYF5W48005",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": []
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00CTYF5W48008",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "title": "*Context restoration*",
    "text": "*Context restoration*: Every turn recovers state cleanly through the view (`aperas tree --view <p>-orchestrator-<role>`) and the thread (`.threads/<role>.md`).",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00CTYF5W48005",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": []
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00CTZJE8C8001",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "title": "**Verification command scope — `npm run verify` is code-only (2026-10-01)**",
    "text": "**Verification command scope — `npm run verify` is code-only (2026-10-01)**: `npm run verify` (even with `verify:slow` separated) is a heavy test suite reserved strictly for code/engine changes. It must never be executed during skill-only tasks. Skill-only verification relies solely on `python3 skills/aperas/scripts/skill_drift.py` and `npm run aperas -- check-links`. Running `verify` for skill edits causes unnecessary hangs, compute waste, and test timeouts.",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00CE8XWZK0001",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": []
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00CTZJGWW0001",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "title": "**Mistaking shadows for the source — root causes of `.threads/` disk access and elevating \"node reference, not file path\" to Philosophy #1 (2026-10-01)**",
    "text": "**Mistaking shadows for the source — root causes of `.threads/` disk access and elevating \"node reference, not file path\" to Philosophy #1 (2026-10-01)**: Detailed analysis of why orchestrators and subagents repeatedly attempt to access `.threads/` using filesystem tools (`ls`, `cat`, `view_file`) in `Aperas/`:",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00CE8XWZK0001",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": [
      "BlockNode:00CTZQR3SG002",
      "BlockNode:00CTZQR3SR000",
      "BlockNode:00CTZQR3SR001",
      "BlockNode:00CTZQR3SR002",
      "BlockNode:00CTZQR3SR003",
      "BlockNode:00CTZQR3SR004"
    ]
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00CTZQR3SG002",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "props": [
      {
        "@id": "BlockNode:00CTZQR3SG002:props:StringProp:00CTZQRB0R000",
        "@type": "StringProp",
        "key": "orderedList",
        "value": "false"
      },
      {
        "@id": "BlockNode:00CTZQR3SG002:props:StringProp:00CTZQRB0R001",
        "@type": "StringProp",
        "key": "startIndex",
        "value": "1"
      }
    ],
    "title": "**Root Cause 1 — The File Mirage (POSIX and Git vocabulary)**",
    "text": "**Root Cause 1 — The File Mirage (POSIX and Git vocabulary)**: The notation `.threads/` (leading dot = hidden directory), `.md` extension, description as \"Git-ignored\" (which applies only to disk files), and phrasing like \"creates in `.threads/grapher.md`\" strongly trigger the LLM's filesystem schema rather than the graph-node schema.",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00CTZJGWW0001",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": []
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00CTZQR3SR000",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "title": "**Root Cause 2 — The Step 1 CLI Tool Void**",
    "text": "**Root Cause 2 — The Step 1 CLI Tool Void**: Step 1 instructs Orchestrators to \"create `## <topic>` and `### <task>` in `.threads/grapher.md`\", but provides zero CLI recipes for resolving thread root IDs or inserting headings without file access. Lacking a graph recipe, agents fall back to `ls` and `cat`.",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00CTZJGWW0001",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": []
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00CTZQR3SR001",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "title": "**Root Cause 3 — Two-repo CWD conflation**",
    "text": "**Root Cause 3 — Two-repo CWD conflation**: Terminal execution is anchored in `$CWD` (`Aperas/`), while graph artifacts are rooted in `AperasKG/artifacts/`. Agents mistakenly resolve relative thread paths against `$CWD`.",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00CTZJGWW0001",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": []
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00CTZQR3SR002",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "title": "**Symptom & philosophical breach — violating Philosophy #1 (\"No inspection of the shadows\")**",
    "text": "**Symptom & philosophical breach — violating Philosophy #1 (\"No inspection of the shadows\")**: Direct file access inspects projected shadows stripped of graph state, backlinks, and view hierarchy.",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00CTZJGWW0001",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": []
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00CTZQR3SR003",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "title": "**Promoting \"Node Reference, Not File Path\" to Section 1 Philosophy**",
    "text": "**Promoting \"Node Reference, Not File Path\" to Section 1 Philosophy**: In v4, \"An `artifacts/**.md` path in your hand is a node reference, not a file path\" was placed in Section 2 as an operational gate. It must be elevated to a core bullet point in Section 1 Philosophy (*The Apeiron is the source*) to govern the entire skill.",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00CTZJGWW0001",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": []
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00CTZQR3SR004",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "title": "**Structural resolution across discipline and CLI runbooks**",
    "text": "**Structural resolution across discipline and CLI runbooks**:",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00CTZJGWW0001",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": [
      "BlockNode:00CTZQR3SR005",
      "BlockNode:00CTZQR3SR006",
      "BlockNode:00CTZQR3SR007"
    ]
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00CTZQR3SR005",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "props": [
      {
        "@id": "BlockNode:00CTZQR3SR005:props:StringProp:00CTZQRB10000",
        "@type": "StringProp",
        "key": "orderedList",
        "value": "false"
      },
      {
        "@id": "BlockNode:00CTZQR3SR005:props:StringProp:00CTZQRB10001",
        "@type": "StringProp",
        "key": "startIndex",
        "value": "1"
      }
    ],
    "title": "00CTZQR3SR005",
    "text": "Reject creating symlinks in `Aperas/` (which merely codifies and facilitates the bad reflex).",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00CTZQR3SR004",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": []
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00CTZQR3SR006",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "title": "00CTZQR3SR006",
    "text": "Provide explicit CLI recipes for Step 1 thread initialization (`aperas show .threads/grapher.md`, `aperas tree .threads/grapher.md`, piping heading inserts).",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00CTZQR3SR004",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": []
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00CTZQR3SR007",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "title": "00CTZQR3SR007",
    "text": "Enforce graph-first traversal via views (`aperas tree --view`) and CLI inspection (`aperas show`, `aperas unfold`).",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00CTZQR3SR004",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": []
  },
  {
