    "title": "**Decision — developers use the global `aperas` shim; the Aperas-repo insiders callouts go away**",
    "text": "**Decision — developers use the global `aperas` shim; the Aperas-repo insiders callouts go away**: (user: \"the callout can go away\", then \"update freeflow for this clean resolution\") There is no distinction between dev and published command forms. Skill bodies and the four role-skill callouts use or show only bare `aperas <verb>`. This supersedes the strengthen-the-callouts decision and the unimplemented repo-script/git and dispatch `Cwd` clauses of [the earlier callout decision](../discussion/aperas-skill.md#id/BlockNode:00CV3WG2C0003), which the shim makes moot. The shim lives outside the repo, in the developer's own environment.",
