  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00CVHQ92ZR001",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "title": "**Resolved — pending items from the shim decision**",
    "text": "**Resolved — pending items from the shim decision**: (1) The Verification Scope line is now one line, `python3 skills/aperas/scripts/skill_drift.py && aperas check-links`, applied as the orchestrator default; the user was asked twice and did not object or choose otherwise. (2) No copy at `/usr/local/bin/aperas` and no fallback pointer in the base skill were added: both Opcode and Antigravity find the shim on their own, and the shim is documented in `design/packaging.md`.",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00CVH7KCP8001",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": []
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00CVJGKZK0001",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "title": "**Decision — document the global `aperas` shim as the dev-environment setup in `packaging.md`**",
    "text": "**Decision — document the global `aperas` shim as the dev-environment setup in `packaging.md`**: (user, direct statement: \"Let's add this shim to packaging.md as a setup for dev env\") The shim and how to install it belong in `packaging.md` as lasting content for anyone developing Aperas from source, not as skill text.",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00CVH7KCP8001",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": [
      "BlockNode:00CVJH9YVG000"
    ]
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00CVJH53Q8001",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "links": [
      {
        "@id": "BlockNode:00CVJH53Q8001:links:Link:00CVJH5A78000",
        "@type": "Link",
        "target": "BlockNode:00CDGTZHSR001",
        "predicate": "[[wikilink]]",
        "props": [
          {
            "@id": "BlockNode:00CVJH53Q8001:links:Link:00CVJH5A78000:props:StringProp:00CVJH5A78001",
            "@type": "StringProp",
            "key": "position",
            "value": "164"
          }
        ]
      }
    ],
    "title": "## Dev environment setup",
    "text": "Developing Aperas from source means running the live TypeScript, not the published bundle. Inside `Aperas/monorepo/` that is `npm run aperas -- <verb> <args>` (see [Topology](#id/BlockNode:00CDGTZHSR001)); a global shim makes bare `aperas <verb> <args>` do the same from any directory, so a session whose working directory is a different project, or an agent harness that does not start in `monorepo/`, still drives the checkout's current source rather than whatever `npm install -g aperas` last installed.",
    "type": "heading",
    "children": [
      "BlockNode:00CVJH53Q8002",
      "BlockNode:00CVJH53Q8003",
      "BlockNode:00CVJH53Q8004",
      "BlockNode:00CVJH53QG002",
      "BlockNode:00CVJH53QG007",
      "BlockNode:00CVJH53QG008",
      "BlockNode:00CVJH53QG009"
    ]
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00CVJH53Q8002",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "title": "The shim is a three-line shell script, `~/.local/bin/aperas`",
    "text": "The shim is a three-line shell script, `~/.local/bin/aperas`:",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00CVJH53Q8001",
    "type": "paragraph",
    "children": []
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00CVJH53Q8003",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "title": "00CVJH53Q8003",
    "text": "```sh\n#!/bin/sh\ncd /home/will/source/Aperas/monorepo && exec env -u LD_LIBRARY_PATH node_modules/.bin/tsx packages/cli/src/aperas.ts \"$@\"\n```",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00CVJH53Q8001",
    "type": "code",
    "children": []
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00CVJH53Q8004",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "title": "00CVJH53Q8004",
    "text": "Replace the path with the checkout's own `monorepo/` directory. Each part has a job:",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00CVJH53Q8001",
    "type": "paragraph",
    "children": [
      "BlockNode:00CVJH53Q8005",
      "BlockNode:00CVJH53Q8006",
      "BlockNode:00CVJH53Q8007",
      "BlockNode:00CVJH53QG000",
      "BlockNode:00CVJH53QG001"
    ]
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00CVJH53Q8005",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "links": [
      {
        "@id": "BlockNode:00CVJH53Q8005:links:Link:00CVJH5A7G000",
        "@type": "Link",
        "target": "BlockNode:00CDY7PGG0001",
        "predicate": "[[wikilink]]",
        "props": [
          {
            "@id": "BlockNode:00CVJH53Q8005:links:Link:00CVJH5A7G000:props:StringProp:00CVJH5A7G001",
            "@type": "StringProp",
            "key": "position",
            "value": "323"
          }
        ]
      }
    ],
    "props": [
      {
        "@id": "BlockNode:00CVJH53Q8005:props:StringProp:00CVJH5A6G000",
        "@type": "StringProp",
        "key": "orderedList",
        "value": "false"
      },
      {
        "@id": "BlockNode:00CVJH53Q8005:props:StringProp:00CVJH5A6G001",
        "@type": "StringProp",
        "key": "startIndex",
        "value": "1"
      }
    ],
    "title": "00CVJH53Q8005",
    "text": "`cd <checkout>/monorepo` — `node_modules/.bin/tsx` and `packages/cli/src/aperas.ts` are relative paths into the workspace, so the shim has to stand in `monorepo/` before it can run either. It also fixes what `process.cwd()` means for the one command that reads it: `aperas service start` resolves its graph from there (see [Workflow](#id/BlockNode:00CDY7PGG0001)), so a service started through the shim always binds to this checkout's graph, whichever directory the shim was called from.",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00CVJH53Q8004",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": []
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00CVJH53Q8006",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "title": "00CVJH53Q8006",
    "text": "`exec` — replaces the shell with the node process instead of running it as a child, so stdin (the `insert`/`update` verbs read piped markdown), signals, and the exit status all pass straight through.",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00CVJH53Q8004",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": []
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00CVJH53Q8007",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "title": "00CVJH53Q8007",
    "text": "`env -u LD_LIBRARY_PATH` — unsets `LD_LIBRARY_PATH` for the node process only. Some hosts (Opcode, for one) export a path to their own bundled libraries, which node picks up in place of the system's and fails at startup with an OpenSSL error that looks like a broken install but is not one. Unsetting it costs nothing where it was never set.",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00CVJH53Q8004",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": []
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00CVJH53QG000",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "title": "00CVJH53QG000",
    "text": "`node_modules/.bin/tsx packages/cli/src/aperas.ts` — runs the CLI entry point's TypeScript source directly through the workspace's own `tsx`, so there is no build step and every edit to `core` or `cli` is live on the next call. A service already running holds the code it started with, so pick up an engine change with `aperas service restart`.",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00CVJH53Q8004",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": []
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00CVJH53QG001",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "title": "00CVJH53QG001",
    "text": "`\"$@\"` — forwards every argument unchanged, quoted so arguments containing spaces or shell metacharacters arrive intact.",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00CVJH53Q8004",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": []
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00CVJH53QG002",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "title": "To install it",
    "text": "To install it:",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00CVJH53Q8001",
    "type": "paragraph",
    "children": [
      "BlockNode:00CVJH53QG003",
      "BlockNode:00CVJH53QG004",
      "BlockNode:00CVJH53QG005",
      "BlockNode:00CVJH53QG006"
    ]
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00CVJH53QG003",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "props": [
      {
        "@id": "BlockNode:00CVJH53QG003:props:StringProp:00CVJH5A6R000",
        "@type": "StringProp",
        "key": "orderedList",
        "value": "true"
      },
      {
        "@id": "BlockNode:00CVJH53QG003:props:StringProp:00CVJH5A6R001",
        "@type": "StringProp",
        "key": "startIndex",
        "value": "1"
      }
    ],
    "title": "00CVJH53QG003",
    "text": "Create the directory if it is missing and write the script: `mkdir -p ~/.local/bin`, then save the three lines above as `~/.local/bin/aperas`.",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00CVJH53QG002",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": []
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00CVJH53QG004",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "title": "Mark it executable",
    "text": "Mark it executable: `chmod +x ~/.local/bin/aperas`.",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00CVJH53QG002",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": []
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00CVJH53QG005",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "title": "00CVJH53QG005",
    "text": "Make sure `~/.local/bin` is on `PATH`. Most login shells add it when the directory exists; an environment that sets its own minimal `PATH` (for example `/usr/local/bin:/usr/bin:/bin`) will not find the shim, and needs the directory added or the shim placed in a directory already on its `PATH`.",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00CVJH53QG002",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": []
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00CVJH53QG006",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "title": "00CVJH53QG006",
    "text": "Dependencies must be installed in the workspace once (`npm install` in `monorepo/`), since the shim relies on its `node_modules/.bin/tsx`.",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00CVJH53QG002",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": []
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00CVJH53QG007",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "title": "A one-command check that it works from anywhere",
    "text": "A one-command check that it works from anywhere:",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00CVJH53Q8001",
    "type": "paragraph",
    "children": []
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00CVJH53QG008",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "title": "00CVJH53QG008",
    "text": "```sh\ncd /tmp && aperas profile list claude\n```",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00CVJH53Q8001",
    "type": "code",
    "children": []
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00CVJH53QG009",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "title": "00CVJH53QG009",
    "text": "It prints the profile's views from the source checkout. `aperas --help` from any directory confirms only that the shim launches, not that the graph is reachable.",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00CVJH53Q8001",
    "type": "paragraph",
    "children": []
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00CVJH6930001",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "links": [
      {
        "@id": "BlockNode:00CVJH6930001:links:Link:00CVJH6F7G000",
        "@type": "Link",
        "target": "BlockNode:00CDGTZHSR001",
        "predicate": "[[wikilink]]",
        "props": [
          {
            "@id": "BlockNode:00CVJH6930001:links:Link:00CVJH6F7G000:props:StringProp:00CVJH6F7G001",
            "@type": "StringProp",
            "key": "position",
            "value": "164"
          }
        ]
      }
    ],
    "title": "## Dev environment setup",
    "text": "Developing Aperas from source means running the live TypeScript, not the published bundle. Inside `Aperas/monorepo/` that is `npm run aperas -- <verb> <args>` (see [Topology](#id/BlockNode:00CDGTZHSR001)); a global shim makes bare `aperas <verb> <args>` do the same from any directory, so a session whose working directory is a different project, or an agent harness that does not start in `monorepo/`, still drives the checkout's current source rather than whatever `npm install -g aperas` last installed.",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00CDDVBXH8001",
    "type": "heading",
    "children": [
      "BlockNode:00CVJH6930002",
      "BlockNode:00CVJH6938000",
      "BlockNode:00CVJH6938001",
      "BlockNode:00CVJH6938007",
      "BlockNode:00CVJH693800C",
      "BlockNode:00CVJH693800D",
      "BlockNode:00CVJH693800E"
    ]
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00CVJH6930002",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "title": "The shim is a three-line shell script, `~/.local/bin/aperas`",
    "text": "The shim is a three-line shell script, `~/.local/bin/aperas`:",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00CVJH6930001",
    "type": "paragraph",
    "children": []
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00CVJH6938000",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "title": "00CVJH6938000",
    "text": "```sh\n#!/bin/sh\ncd /home/will/source/Aperas/monorepo && exec env -u LD_LIBRARY_PATH node_modules/.bin/tsx packages/cli/src/aperas.ts \"$@\"\n```",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00CVJH6930001",
    "type": "code",
    "children": []
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00CVJH6938001",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "title": "00CVJH6938001",
    "text": "Replace the path with the checkout's own `monorepo/` directory. Each part has a job:",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00CVJH6930001",
    "type": "paragraph",
    "children": [
      "BlockNode:00CVJH6938002",
      "BlockNode:00CVJH6938003",
      "BlockNode:00CVJH6938004",
      "BlockNode:00CVJH6938005",
      "BlockNode:00CVJH6938006"
    ]
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00CVJH6938002",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "links": [
      {
        "@id": "BlockNode:00CVJH6938002:links:Link:00CVJH6F7G002",
        "@type": "Link",
        "target": "BlockNode:00CDY7PGG0001",
        "predicate": "[[wikilink]]",
        "props": [
          {
            "@id": "BlockNode:00CVJH6938002:links:Link:00CVJH6F7G002:props:StringProp:00CVJH6F7G003",
            "@type": "StringProp",
            "key": "position",
            "value": "323"
          }
        ]
      }
    ],
    "props": [
      {
        "@id": "BlockNode:00CVJH6938002:props:StringProp:00CVJH6F70000",
        "@type": "StringProp",
        "key": "orderedList",
        "value": "false"
      },
      {
        "@id": "BlockNode:00CVJH6938002:props:StringProp:00CVJH6F70001",
        "@type": "StringProp",
        "key": "startIndex",
        "value": "1"
      }
    ],
    "title": "00CVJH6938002",
    "text": "`cd <checkout>/monorepo` — `node_modules/.bin/tsx` and `packages/cli/src/aperas.ts` are relative paths into the workspace, so the shim has to stand in `monorepo/` before it can run either. It also fixes what `process.cwd()` means for the one command that reads it: `aperas service start` resolves its graph from there (see [Workflow](#id/BlockNode:00CDY7PGG0001)), so a service started through the shim always binds to this checkout's graph, whichever directory the shim was called from.",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00CVJH6938001",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": []
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00CVJH6938003",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "title": "00CVJH6938003",
    "text": "`exec` — replaces the shell with the node process instead of running it as a child, so stdin (the `insert`/`update` verbs read piped markdown), signals, and the exit status all pass straight through.",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00CVJH6938001",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": []
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00CVJH6938004",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "title": "00CVJH6938004",
    "text": "`env -u LD_LIBRARY_PATH` — unsets `LD_LIBRARY_PATH` for the node process only. Some hosts (Opcode, for one) export a path to their own bundled libraries, which node picks up in place of the system's and fails at startup with an OpenSSL error that looks like a broken install but is not one. Unsetting it costs nothing where it was never set.",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00CVJH6938001",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": []
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00CVJH6938005",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "title": "00CVJH6938005",
    "text": "`node_modules/.bin/tsx packages/cli/src/aperas.ts` — runs the CLI entry point's TypeScript source directly through the workspace's own `tsx`, so there is no build step and every edit to `core` or `cli` is live on the next call. A service already running holds the code it started with, so pick up an engine change with `aperas service restart`.",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00CVJH6938001",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": []
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00CVJH6938006",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "title": "00CVJH6938006",
    "text": "`\"$@\"` — forwards every argument unchanged, quoted so arguments containing spaces or shell metacharacters arrive intact.",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00CVJH6938001",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": []
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00CVJH6938007",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "title": "To install it",
    "text": "To install it:",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00CVJH6930001",
    "type": "paragraph",
    "children": [
      "BlockNode:00CVJH6938008",
      "BlockNode:00CVJH6938009",
      "BlockNode:00CVJH693800A",
      "BlockNode:00CVJH693800B"
    ]
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00CVJH6938008",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "props": [
      {
        "@id": "BlockNode:00CVJH6938008:props:StringProp:00CVJH6F78000",
        "@type": "StringProp",
        "key": "orderedList",
        "value": "true"
      },
      {
        "@id": "BlockNode:00CVJH6938008:props:StringProp:00CVJH6F78001",
        "@type": "StringProp",
        "key": "startIndex",
        "value": "1"
      }
    ],
    "title": "00CVJH6938008",
    "text": "Create the directory if it is missing and write the script: `mkdir -p ~/.local/bin`, then save the three lines above as `~/.local/bin/aperas`.",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00CVJH6938007",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": []
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00CVJH6938009",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "title": "Mark it executable",
    "text": "Mark it executable: `chmod +x ~/.local/bin/aperas`.",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00CVJH6938007",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": []
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00CVJH693800A",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "title": "00CVJH693800A",
    "text": "Make sure `~/.local/bin` is on `PATH`. Most login shells add it when the directory exists; an environment that sets its own minimal `PATH` (for example `/usr/local/bin:/usr/bin:/bin`) will not find the shim, and needs the directory added or the shim placed in a directory already on its `PATH`.",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00CVJH6938007",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": []
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00CVJH693800B",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "title": "00CVJH693800B",
    "text": "Dependencies must be installed in the workspace once (`npm install` in `monorepo/`), since the shim relies on its `node_modules/.bin/tsx`.",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00CVJH6938007",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": []
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00CVJH693800C",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "title": "A one-command check that it works from anywhere",
    "text": "A one-command check that it works from anywhere:",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00CVJH6930001",
    "type": "paragraph",
    "children": []
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00CVJH693800D",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "title": "00CVJH693800D",
    "text": "```sh\ncd /tmp && aperas profile list claude\n```",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00CVJH6930001",
    "type": "code",
    "children": []
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00CVJH693800E",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "title": "00CVJH693800E",
    "text": "It prints the profile's views from the source checkout. `aperas --help` from any directory confirms only that the shim launches, not that the graph is reachable.",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00CVJH6930001",
    "type": "paragraph",
    "children": []
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00CVJH9YVG000",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "links": [
      {
        "@id": "BlockNode:00CVJH9YVG000:links:Link:00CVJHA4R8000",
