    ],
    "title": "00CVJH9YVG000",
    "text": "Promoted to [Dev environment setup](../design/packaging.md#id/BlockNode:00CVJH6930001)",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00CVJGKZK0001",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": []
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00CVJNK3K8001",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "title": "**Decision — update the skills now**",
    "text": "**Decision — update the skills now**: (user, direct statement: \"Now, update the skills\") Proceed with the skill edits under the decisions above: bodies use bare `aperas <verb>`, the four Aperas-repo insiders callouts are removed, and the shim is documented in `design/packaging.md`. The Verification Scope line returning to one line stays an orchestrator default the user has not objected to or confirmed.",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00CVH7KCP8001",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": []
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00CVJPV978001",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "title": "**Friction — ApeironNgn service dropped between commands**",
    "text": "**Friction — ApeironNgn service dropped between commands**: Twice the service was not running when a command ran (`aperas project` and an `aperas insert` both failed with \"No ApeironNgn service running. Start one with: aperas service start\"). The first `aperas service start` reported \"did not become ready in time\" while the service was still loading its 31k quads; a retry about 20 seconds later succeeded. The second time, `aperas service start` reported it already running. No config was changed.",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00CVH7KCP8001",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": [
      "BlockNode:00CVN8M96R001"
    ]
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00CVJR6X9R001",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "props": [
      {
        "@id": "BlockNode:00CVJR6X9R001:props:StringProp:00CVJR7368000",
        "@type": "StringProp",
        "key": "orderedList",
        "value": "false"
      },
      {
        "@id": "BlockNode:00CVJR6X9R001:props:StringProp:00CVJR7368001",
        "@type": "StringProp",
        "key": "startIndex",
        "value": "1"
      }
    ],
    "title": "**Finding — site map of `npm run aperas` in `skills/` (coder survey)**",
    "text": "**Finding — site map of `npm run aperas` in `skills/` (coder survey)**: 27 hits in 4 groups. (1) Four insiders callouts to delete: `skills/aperas/SKILL.md` lines 14-18 (a blockquote with a fenced `npm run aperas -- <verb> ...` block), and one-line blockquotes at `aperas-orchestrator/SKILL.md:18`, `aperas-coder/SKILL.md:17`, `aperas-grapher/SKILL.md:17`. (2) 22 body uses to change to bare `aperas`: `aperas/SKILL.md` at 139, 148 (two), 174, 175, 178, 181, 184, 187, 279, 283; `aperas-orchestrator/SKILL.md` at 122 and 153; `aperas-coder/SKILL.md` at 28, 42, 57, 63, 69; `aperas-grapher/SKILL.md` at 28, 40, 55, 61, 67. The `npm run verify` mentions (base 282, orchestrator 149 and 155) are a real repo script and stay. (3) `skills/aperas/scripts/aperas_gate.py:72` only names the form in a deny-message string (\"Running any `aperas`/`npm run aperas` command opens this gate\"); the script never invokes the CLI and its `--mark` matcher `*aperas*` is a substring, so both forms match and the string can drop `npm run aperas`. (4) `skills/aperas-workspace/graph-sandbox.sh:27` (`aperas() { (cd \"$MONOREPO\" && npm run --silent aperas -- \"$@\"); }`) is the only code that executes the `npm run` form; it is a dev-only sandbox for mutating evals, tracked but not bundled and with no SKILL.md. Not sites: `aperas/references/mechanics.md` (already bare), `show_node.py`, `skill_drift.py`, and the oxigraph, solidjs and terminusdb skills.",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00CVH7KCP8001",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": []
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00CVJR6X9R002",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "title": "**Finding — `kg-doc-ingest` points at the callout being removed**",
    "text": "**Finding — `kg-doc-ingest` points at the callout being removed**: `skills/kg-doc-ingest/SKILL.md` line 16 says \"All commands run from `Aperas/monorepo/` as `aperas <verb> <args>` (see the `aperas` skill's own insider note on today's actual invocation)\". Once the base callout is gone the parenthetical points at nothing, and the `Aperas/monorepo/` working-directory claim is wrong for the global shim, which runs from any directory. It contains no `npm run`, so it is not one of the 27 sites, but it needs editing in the same pass. The skill ships to end users (it is in the bundled list), so a stale reference there is user-visible. `skill_drift.py` does not compare this file, so the edit needs no v4.3 delta entry.",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00CVH7KCP8001",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": []
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00CVJR6X9R003",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "title": "**Finding — skills are symlinked and never parsed by build or tests**",
    "text": "**Finding — skills are symlinked and never parsed by build or tests**: `.claude/skills/X` and `.agents/skills/X` are symlinks (`.claude/skills/X -> .agents/skills/X -> skills/X`), so one edit under `skills/` covers every host with no mirror to sync. The build (`monorepo/packages/cli/build.mjs`, lines about 58-71) and `kgSkill.ts` (lines 25-62) copy the bundled skill directories byte for byte and never read their text, and no test reads skill text. The only thing an edit can trip is `skill_drift.py`, which is the verification the skill-only task loop already names.",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00CVH7KCP8001",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": []
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00CVJR6X9R004",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "title": "**Finding — the `aperas skill` command description lists two skills while the installer ships five**",
    "text": "**Finding — the `aperas skill` command description lists two skills while the installer ships five**: `monorepo/packages/cli/src/aperas.ts` line 53 describes the command as installing \"(aperas, kg-doc-ingest)\", but `kgSkill.ts` line 25 lists `aperas`, `aperas-orchestrator`, `aperas-grapher`, `aperas-coder` and `kg-doc-ingest`. Pre-existing and unrelated to the `npm run` change; recorded here because the survey found it, and promoted to an issue under the rule that every defect or gap is promoted in a Filing Turn.",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00CVH7KCP8001",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": [
      "BlockNode:00CVN8NN5R001"
    ]
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00CVJR6X9R005",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "title": "**Resolved — what the v4.3 delta covers (recorded after the coder's edit)**",
    "text": "**Resolved — what the v4.3 delta covers (recorded after the coder's edit)**: `skill_drift.py` compares the live four `SKILL.md` files (the base plus the three `aperas-*` role skills; `kg-doc-ingest` is not compared) against the latest snapshot plus every delta above it, unit by unit (one unit per list item or blank-line-separated paragraph longer than 40 characters, fences stripped). Today that comparison is clean (0 added, 0 dropped). The text `npm run aperas` appears in 25 live recorded units (4 in the v4 snapshot, 19 in the v4.1 delta, 2 in the v4.2 delta) and in 25 file units (base 10, coder 6, grapher 6, orchestrator 3); the \"52 BlockNodes\" count is a raw grep of the store and also counts tombstoned nodes, older snapshots and Freeflow text. Rewriting those lines to bare `aperas` makes each old recorded unit read as DROPPED and each new unit as ADDED unless a v4.3 delta records it, with a `Supersedes:` marker naming the superseded block id. Four of the old units are the callouts (v4 snapshot ids 00CS1593MG006, 00CS1593N001W, 00CS1593N8019 and 00CS1593NG013); they have no replacement text, so the delta would need an entry whose only content is `Supersedes:` lines (the checker strips those markers before comparing, so such an entry leaves nothing to read as dropped; this is read from the checker's code and not yet run). Prose-only units that mention the form (for example the v4.1 `.threads/` callout, the v4.1 Orchestrator Verification item and the v4.2 Resolution Rule and Skill-only changes items) are in the same set. The delta follows the coder's edit and must exist before the step 7 drift check can pass. Resolution: the v4.3 delta records the 19 ADDED units with `Supersedes:` lines and retires the four callouts and the other unaccounted v4.1 and v4.2 blocks in entries made of `Supersedes:` lines only; `skill_drift.py` now reports 0 ADDED unrecorded and 0 DROPPED unaccounted.",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00CVH7KCP8001",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": []
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00CVJR6X9R006",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "title": "**Resolved — scope questions from the coder**",
