    "title": "## v4.3 additions — delta on the v4 snapshot",
    "text": "Records the v4.3 edits to the four skills. The first standardizes every command in the skill bodies on the bare `aperas <verb>` form and removes the four \"Aperas-repo insiders\" callouts, decided in [Standard `aperas` command in skill bodies](#id/BlockNode:00CVH7KCP8001) and settled by [Decision — developers use the global `aperas` shim](#id/BlockNode:00CVHQ92ZR000). The second is the wording edit decided in [Skill wording update for v4.3](#id/BlockNode:00CVKQDJ2G001): friction entries collect any trouble under `**Friction — <topic>**`, each Question carries its own topic, the orchestrator's source-reading gate covers checking, assessing and reviewing a result or claim, and the four `Status:` lines move to v4.3 with one `Status` entry per skill. The third is a guard in `skill_drift.py`: it exits nonzero on a Status mismatch, an unrecorded addition or an unaccounted drop, so the newest delta's version must equal the four `Status:` lines. The fourth is the drift-expectation wording: the base and Orchestrator verification lines run `skill_drift.py` and `aperas check-links` as two separate commands and say drift is expected to fail at Step 7 naming the edited units, the Coder skill says that failure is the expected sequence and is not the Coder's to clear, and the Grapher skill gains a \"Recording a skill delta\" subsection, decided in [Decision — write the Grapher skill's Recording a skill delta subsection and file the `aperas.ts` mismatch](#id/BlockNode:00CVMGWF48003). The fifth is the promotion wording, decided in [Decision — issue promotion belongs to the Filing Turn, other promotions to the Finishing Turn](#id/BlockNode:00CVMH0MB0001): defects and gaps are promoted to `issues/` in the Filing Turn, and recurring patterns and settled outcomes in the Finishing Turn, across the base task loop, the Orchestrator's Asks and the Grapher's Filing and Finishing Turns. The sixth is the one-minute rule, decided in [Decision — the one-minute rule applies to every agent, including the orchestrator, and the orientation is to bubble up](#id/BlockNode:00CVPZKPN8000): the base bullet reads \"One minute is the limit on anything that does not answer, for every role\", the Coder and Grapher skills restate the subagent half, and the Orchestrator skill gains the callout \"Stuck Things Go to the User\". Each entry that rewrites recorded text carries a `Supersedes:` line naming the v4, v4.1 or v4.2 block it replaces; entries with no new text only retire blocks. Entries first written for an earlier edit in this delta were updated in place rather than superseded ([Default — the v4.3 delta entries already recorded are updated in place](#id/BlockNode:00CVKV9DPG005)).",
