    "type": "listItem",
    "children": [
      "BlockNode:00CVJXQWNR00X",
      "BlockNode:00CVJXQWNR00Y"
    ]
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00CVJXQWNR00X",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "title": "00CVJXQWNR00X",
    "text": "```bash\npython3 skills/aperas/scripts/skill_drift.py\naperas check-links\n```",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00CVJXQWNR00W",
    "type": "code",
    "children": []
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00CVJXQWNR00Y",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "title": "00CVJXQWNR00Y",
    "text": "Run them as two commands. `skill_drift.py` is expected to fail at Step 7, naming the edited units, because the Grapher has not yet recorded the delta; it is expected to pass after the Grapher's Step 8. Do not treat that failure as a Coder defect. Running `npm run verify` on skill modifications is a severe process violation that leads to test timeouts and compute waste.",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00CVJXQWNR00W",
    "type": "paragraph",
    "children": []
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00CVJXTDEG001",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "title": "00CVJXTDEG001",
    "text": "---",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00CVJXQWNR005",
    "type": "thematicBreak",
    "children": []
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00CVK447WR001",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "title": "### Grapher skill has no skill-record delta or version-bump protocol",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00CE8XWZK0001",
    "type": "heading",
    "children": [
      "BlockNode:00CVK452T8000",
      "BlockNode:00CVK452T8003",
      "BlockNode:00CVM3HRAR001"
    ]
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00CVK452T8000",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "props": [
      {
        "@id": "BlockNode:00CVK452T8000:props:StringProp:00CVK45928000",
        "@type": "StringProp",
        "key": "orderedList",
        "value": "false"
      },
      {
        "@id": "BlockNode:00CVK452T8000:props:StringProp:00CVK45928001",
        "@type": "StringProp",
        "key": "startIndex",
        "value": "1"
      }
    ],
    "title": "**Finding — the skill/Status version mismatch exposes a gap in the Grapher skill**",
    "text": "**Finding — the skill/Status version mismatch exposes a gap in the Grapher skill**: (user: \"That mismatch shows a gap in the Grapher skill\") The v4.3 delta was recorded while all four skills' `Status:` lines still say v4.2. The grapher did not decide whether to bump them and asked the orchestrator instead, because nothing it was given says who bumps `Status:`, or that a delta titled with a new version needs one `Status` entry per skill. Only the v4.2 delta carried `Status` entries (four); the v4.1 delta carried none and the files stayed at v4. If the files are bumped without matching entries, drift reports four unrecorded additions; the reverse order, as here, is invisible to the checker because it never reads a `Status:` line.",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00CVK447WR001",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": [
      "BlockNode:00CVK452T8001",
      "BlockNode:00CVK452T8002"
    ]
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00CVK452T8001",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "props": [
      {
        "@id": "BlockNode:00CVK452T8001:props:StringProp:00CVK4592G000",
        "@type": "StringProp",
        "key": "orderedList",
        "value": "false"
      },
      {
        "@id": "BlockNode:00CVK452T8001:props:StringProp:00CVK4592G001",
        "@type": "StringProp",
        "key": "startIndex",
        "value": "1"
      }
    ],
    "title": "00CVK452T8001",
    "text": "A search of the four `SKILL.md` files for `delta`, `supersede`, `bump` and `version` finds only the four `Status:` lines themselves. The `Supersedes:` convention, the rule that a removed unit needs a `Supersedes:`-only entry, and the checker's folding of a `---` under a bullet into that bullet's unit are not in the Grapher skill; the grapher worked them out by reading the drift checker's code and its output.",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00CVK452T8000",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": []
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00CVK452T8002",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "tombstonedAt": "2026-10-02T09:29:15.043Z",
    "title": "00CVK452T8002",
    "text": "The same turn also showed that the Ask had to name the version label, which the Grapher skill would otherwise leave to chance.",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00CVK452T8000",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": []
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00CVK452T8003",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "title": "**Open — who bumps `Status:` and when**",
    "text": "**Open — who bumps `Status:` and when**: This item first asked what the Grapher skill should say about `Status:` bumps, the delta's required shape and the `---` folding gotcha. The last two are now written or moot: the Grapher skill's \"Recording a skill delta\" subsection gives the delta's shape (one `Supersedes:` line per replaced block, a `Supersedes:`-only block for a removal), the order of work and the 40-character limit, a `Status` entry per bumped skill sits in its drift section, and the `---` gotcha is gone because the checker's separator rule handles it. Still unwritten in any skill: who bumps a `Status:` line and when, with the skill edit or with the delta.",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00CVK447WR001",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": [
      "BlockNode:00CVN8KDW0001"
    ]
  },
  {
