      }
    ],
    "title": "**Finding — `check-links` and the insert link summary miss an id link whose target does not exist**",
    "text": "**Finding — `check-links` and the insert link summary miss an id link whose target does not exist**: An orchestrator Ask (`BlockNode:00CVJV0S7G002`) carried the link `[...](../discussion/aperas-skill.md#id/BlockNode:00CVJPV978002)`, and no such node existed (`aperas show BlockNode:00CVJPV978002` failed with \"Node ... not found\"). The link record's `target` held that id. The insert reported \"Links: 3 resolved, 0 dangling, 3 changed\", and a later `aperas check-links` reported a clean pass (3586 live blocks, 0 discrepancies) while the link was still in place. The text was corrected by hand afterwards, so the broken state is gone and a repro is still needed.",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00CVKEK84G001",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": [
      "BlockNode:00CVKFYEF8001"
    ]
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00CVKEPTWG000",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "title": "**Decision — file the `check-links` miss as an issue**",
    "text": "**Decision — file the `check-links` miss as an issue**: (user: \"The `check-links` should be filed as an issue\") The grapher files it under the linking concern with the evidence above, and confirms the repro with a throwaway node in its own thread, removing it afterwards.",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00CVKEK84G001",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": []
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00CVKFWNB8001",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "links": [
      {
        "@id": "BlockNode:00CVKFWNB8001:links:Link:00CVKFWW38000",
        "@type": "Link",
        "target": "BlockNode:00CGMWQ6T0001",
        "predicate": "[[wikilink]]",
        "props": [
          {
            "@id": "BlockNode:00CVKFWNB8001:links:Link:00CVKFWW38000:props:StringProp:00CVKFWW38001",
            "@type": "StringProp",
            "key": "position",
            "value": "1508"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "@id": "BlockNode:00CVKFWNB8001:links:Link:00CVKFWW38002",
        "@type": "Link",
        "target": "BlockNode:00CGN6GJVG000",
        "predicate": "[[wikilink]]",
        "props": [
          {
            "@id": "BlockNode:00CVKFWNB8001:links:Link:00CVKFWW38002:props:StringProp:00CVKFWW38003",
            "@type": "StringProp",
            "key": "position",
            "value": "1666"
          }
        ]
      }
    ],
    "title": "**`check-links` and the write-time link summary treat an id link to a nonexistent node as resolved — the `aperas://id/` branch of `resolveDeepPathDetail` never checks the id exists**",
    "text": "**`check-links` and the write-time link summary treat an id link to a nonexistent node as resolved — the `aperas://id/` branch of `resolveDeepPathDetail` never checks the id exists**: confirmed live, reproduced on the first attempt. A throwaway list item in a thread carried `[x](../discussion/aperas-skill.md#id/BlockNode:00ZZZZZZZZ999)`, where `aperas show BlockNode:00ZZZZZZZZ999` fails with \"Node ... not found\". The insert reported \"Links: 1 resolved, 0 dangling, 1 changed\", the stored node held a `Link` whose `target` was the nonexistent id (predicate `[[wikilink]]`, position 17), and `aperas check-links` (also with `--verbose`) reported \"Clean pass: 0 link integrity discrepancies\" both before and after the insert. Root cause traced in the code: `resolveDeepPathDetail` (`resolveCreate.ts:237`) answers any `aperas://id/<ID>` ref with `{ id: <ID> }` by pure string slicing, with no store lookup; `resolveFragmentCode` (`artifacts.ts`) routes every `#id/<ID>` fragment through it, so `resolveBlockLinks` counts the code as resolved (the `dangling` counter and the `danglingRef` stash are only reached on a null result) and writes a `Link` to a node that is not there. `checkLinkIntegrity` (`linkIntegrity.ts`) calls the same `resolveOneCode` and reports only a code that resolves and is missing from `.links`; here it resolves, is present in `.links`, and so passes, so the check cannot see the miss by construction. Both blind spots are one defect, and it falls outside every mechanism listed in [the open link-persistence issue](#id/BlockNode:00CGMWQ6T0001) (those lose a link that should exist; this keeps a link that should not) and outside the scope [Link Integrity Checking built](#id/BlockNode:00CGN6GJVG000) records for the check, which leaves an unresolved code alone. Not tested: a bare `BlockNode:<ID>` or `[[<ID>]]` direct-id form, a link whose target exists but is tombstoned, and a typo'd id whose shape is invalid. Fix direction, not yet implemented and not yet agreed: verify target existence (live, non-tombstoned) at the link-resolution layer (`resolveFragmentCode` / `resolveOneCode`), not inside `resolveDeepPathDetail`, since that function's `aperas://id/` pass-through is presumably relied on by callers that want the raw id back, so a missing id then follows the existing dangling path (warn, count, stash in `danglingRef`); and add a check-links pass that flags any live `Link` whose `target` is not a live node, which would also catch targets tombstoned after the link was written. `verify.ts` would want a fixture with a nonexistent id link asserting a nonzero dangling count and a check-links discrepancy.",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00CDBYV5A8002",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": []
  },
  {
