    "title": "**Finding — the coder's survey of the v4.3 skill edit sites**",
    "text": "**Finding — the coder's survey of the v4.3 skill edit sites**: The checker finds the recorded deltas by title in `BlockNode.jsonld` and orders them by version; the Status guard fits in `main()` right after the recorded roots are chosen, using the four skill files the checker already receives (which exclude `kg-doc-ingest`). The checker exits 0 on every finding today, and only text references rely on that: the chain `skill_drift.py && aperas check-links` in the orchestrator and base skills. Nothing in `packages/cli`, tests, hooks or CI reads the `Status:` lines or the checker; the bundle only copies the skill directories, and its stale `dist/skills/` copy (v3.0) is git-ignored and out of the guard's reach. The guard would fail the first time it runs, until the four `Status:` lines move to v4.3 with the same edit.",
