    "title": "**Finding — the wording sites the v4.3 edit touches, by file and line**",
    "text": "**Finding — the wording sites the v4.3 edit touches, by file and line**: (coder survey; lines as of the staged `skills/` at survey time, which the edit will move) Friction wording, `Tool gap` lead-ins: `skills/aperas/SKILL.md:159` and `:160` (Report template lines `**Tool gap — <what>**`, `**Tool gap — <what else>**`), `:192` (Core Thread Disciplines \"Record friction\" bullet, \"distinct `**Tool gap — <topic>**` lead-ins\"), `:193` (Ask-back bullet, \"unexpected tool failures\"); `skills/aperas-coder/SKILL.md:47` (template) and `:128` (\"Results and tool friction not captured in subturns are permanently lost\"); `skills/aperas-grapher/SKILL.md:45` (template, same text as coder:47) and `:91` (\"File every tool gap reported by either role under the appropriate tool concern\"); `skills/aperas-orchestrator/SKILL.md:71` (\"Record any friction you encounter yourself into Freeflow as well\"), with no `Tool gap` string anywhere in that file. Five `Tool gap —` lead-in lines in all (base 159, 160; coder 47; grapher 45) plus the base:192 rule. `skills/aperas/SKILL.md:22` (TOC) and `:287` (`### Open Tool Gaps`) name tool gaps as a topic, not as the lead-in.",
