    "title": "**Finding — the bare `**Question**` sites and the source-reading gate sites**",
    "text": "**Finding — the bare `**Question**` sites and the source-reading gate sites**: (coder survey) Bare `**Question**` with no topic: `skills/aperas/SKILL.md:158` (template) and `:193` (prose, \"via a `**Question**` in its Report\"); `skills/aperas-coder/SKILL.md:46` (template), `:89` (\"formulate a `**Question**` in your Report\") and `:99` (the Report Format for Questions block); `skills/aperas-grapher/SKILL.md:44` (template; that skill has no prose paragraph about asking back); the orchestrator skill has none. The source-reading gate: `skills/aperas/SKILL.md:116` (Orchestrator Reads cell, \"Graph, threads, **and source code/diffs/tests during Verification**\"), `:121-123` (the `[!CRITICAL]` Orchestrator Role Gate, with \"**ONLY at the Verification stage**\" on `:123`), `:133` (step-7 entry, no `only` in it); `skills/aperas-orchestrator/SKILL.md:29-34` (the same callout under `### What You Do NOT Do Initially`, \"**ONLY at the Verification stage**\" on `:34`), `:100-101` (step-7 entry, no `only`), `:140-157` (the Verification Protocol section). The word \"only\" in this sense appears at exactly two lines (base:123, orchestrator:34); every other site carries the limit by implication (\"during Verification\", \"Step 7\"). Related but not the same gate and not to be edited: `skills/aperas-grapher/SKILL.md:84` (\"Touch source code only to pinpoint entry points\"), `skills/aperas-coder/SKILL.md:82` (the survey-turn \"DO NOT modify source code\"), and `skills/aperas-orchestrator/SKILL.md:38` and `:166` (skill-file edits go to the Coder).",
