    "title": "**Finding — how the checker finds the deltas and where the Status guard fits**",
    "text": "**Finding — how the checker finds the deltas and where the Status guard fits**: (coder survey of `skills/aperas/scripts/skill_drift.py`) It reads the raw store `AperasKG/Apeiron/BlockNode.jsonld` (`find_graph_dir`, `load_blocks`, `:48-76`) and never calls the `aperas` CLI. `SNAPSHOT_RE` and `DELTA_RE` (`:41-42`) match a node's `title`; `version_of` (`:131-133`) takes the first `v...` token, so `## v4.2 additions — delta on the v4 snapshot` gives `(4, 2)` and the snapshot title gives `(4,)`, with `(-1,)` for no match. `recorded_roots` (`:136-157`) collects every non-tombstoned snapshot and delta, takes the newest snapshot as baseline, and returns that snapshot plus every delta at or after it, sorted by version; it returns `[]` with no snapshot. It resolves four roots today (the v4 snapshot and the v4.1, v4.2 and v4.3 deltas). The guard fits in `main()` at `:212-214`, after `roots = recorded_roots(blocks)` and the \"no snapshot or delta sections found\" exit; the newest delta is the last delta entry of `roots` (or the snapshot when there is none), and `skills = find_skill_files()` at `:210` already holds the four files (`aperas/SKILL.md` plus `sorted(glob(\"aperas-*/SKILL.md\"))`, `:56-65`), which exclude `kg-doc-ingest`, so a guard over `skills` is automatically the four-file set while a repo-wide `Status:` search would fail on `kg-doc-ingest`'s `v0`. Versions compare as tuples after trimming trailing zeros, so `(4,)` equals `(4, 0)`. The comparison is independent of `--added` and `--dropped`: the printing blocks are gated by `both or args.added` (`:228`) and `both or args.dropped` (`:241`), so where it runs is a design choice. Constraints the guard must respect: the \"superseded, accounted for\" list (`accounted`, `:248`) is 170 lines on every run and is not a finding, so it must stay out of the exit status; the header docstring (`:14`, `:25-30`) and the `--added` and `--dropped` help text would need to state the exit rule. Existing open issues on the same checker that the edit does not close: [`skill_drift.py` only checks one direction](../issues/aperas-skill.md#id/BlockNode:00CN89ERE8000) and [`norm()` runs before the `Supersedes:` strip](../issues/aperas-skill.md#id/BlockNode:00CNX13PMR001), the second of which bears on new delta entries carrying a `Supersedes:` line.",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00CVKQDJ2G001",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": []
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00CVKY8V6R005",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "title": "**Finding — the checker's exit status and who relies on it**",
    "text": "**Finding — the checker's exit status and who relies on it**: (coder survey) `main()` has no return value and no `sys.exit(<int>)`; `if __name__ == \"__main__\": main()` (`:265-266`). Every finding path (unrecorded additions, unaccounted drops, accounted-for supersessions) only prints, so the exit is always 0. The only nonzero exits are `sys.exit(\"<message>\")` (exit 1, message on stderr) at `:53` (no `AperasKG/Apeiron`), `:64` (missing skill file) and `:214` (no snapshot or delta), plus argparse's exit 2 on a bad flag. The counts for an any-finding exit are already computed: `len(missing)` at `:230-233` on the added side and `len(unaccounted)` at `:249` on the dropped side. Callers relying on exit 0 are three text references and no executable caller: `skills/aperas-orchestrator/SKILL.md:150` and `skills/aperas/SKILL.md:133` and `:277` (`... && aperas check-links`, so a nonzero exit would skip `check-links`), and `skills/aperas-grapher/SKILL.md:157-159` (run bare and with each flag, no chaining). Making the exit nonzero turns the step-7 verification chain from always-passes into a real gate; today it also passes with a stale v4.2 Status line beside a v4.3 delta.",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00CVKQDJ2G001",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": []
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00CVKY8V6R006",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "title": "**Finding — nothing outside the skill files reads the `Status:` lines or the checker**",
    "text": "**Finding — nothing outside the skill files reads the `Status:` lines or the checker**: (coder survey) Grep for `skill_drift` and `skill-drift` outside `AperasKG/artifacts/` finds only the skill text lines above and the script's own docstring. No test in `monorepo/packages/*/src` or test directories, no script in `skills/`, no CI config (no `.github`, no `.husky`), no hook, and no `package.json` script (`monorepo/package.json:14` `verify` runs `packages/cli/src/verify.ts`, which does not mention it). The only other script under `skills/aperas/scripts/`, `aperas_gate.py`, is an unrelated PreToolUse hook that never reads `Status:` or calls the checker. In `monorepo/packages/cli`, `src/kgSkill.ts:23` lists the five skills and `runInstall` (`:46-67`) copies each directory with `cpSync` without opening a `SKILL.md`; `build.mjs:75-79` (`BUNDLED_SKILLS`) copies `skills/<name>` to `dist/skills/<name>`, taking `skill_drift.py` along unread. `monorepo/packages/cli/dist/skills/` is a stale build output (Status lines still `v3.0`, `kg-doc-ingest` `v0`), git-ignored (`monorepo/.gitignore:11`, `git ls-files` returns nothing) and out of the guard's reach, because `find_skill_files` resolves `Path(__file__).parents[2]`, the `skills/` that holds the script. `.agents/skills/<name>` and `.claude/skills/<name>` are symlinks to `../../skills/<name>`, so `skills/` alone is the editing target, and the agent definitions under `.agents/agents/` and `.claude/agents/` list skills to preload but carry no version text. `packages/core`, `packages/web` and `verify.ts` do not mention `Status:`.",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00CVKQDJ2G001",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": []
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00CVKY8V6R007",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
