    "title": "**Resolved — the v4.3 delta records the whole edit, and the drift check passes**",
    "text": "**Resolved — the v4.3 delta records the whole edit, and the drift check passes**: [`## v4.3 additions`](#id/BlockNode:00CVJXQWNG001) now carries four `Status` entries (one per skill, each superseding its v4.2 `Status` unit, as [Decision — the Status entries are four, one per skill](#id/BlockNode:00CVM0R5A0002) decided), twelve wording entries covering the 24 units the drift check reported as unrecorded, each with a `Supersedes:` line naming the v4 snapshot block it replaces, and its intro now covers the bare-`aperas` edit, the wording edit and the guard. The three entries first written for the bare-`aperas` edit (`00CVJXQWNG005`, `00CVJXQWNR00J`, `00CVJXQWNR009`) were updated in place, as [Default — the v4.3 delta entries already recorded are updated in place](#id/BlockNode:00CVKV9DPG005) set out. No `Supersedes:`-only entry was needed: every one of the 13 dropped units has a replacement. `skill_drift.py` exits 0 with 0 Status findings, 0 ADDED but unrecorded and 0 DROPPED unaccounted, against the 24 and 13 that [the orchestrator's verification](#id/BlockNode:00CVM0R5A0001) counted before the delta was updated.",
