    "title": "**Verification — the second v4.3 skill edit inspected; one wording fix remains**",
    "text": "**Verification — the second v4.3 skill edit inspected; one wording fix remains**: The orchestrator read the new Grapher subsection \"Recording a skill delta\" (six items), the Filing and Finishing Turn wording (defects and gaps to `issues/` in the Filing Turn; recurring patterns and settled outcomes in the Finishing Turn), the new Coder-skill item, the two-command verification lines in the orchestrator and base skills (no `&&` chain of the two commands is left), and the `file_units` change (a lone `---` line now ends a paragraph, with the reason in the docstring). `skill_drift.py` exits 1 as expected: 0 Status, 18 ADDED unrecorded, 9 DROPPED unaccounted, 183 accounted for. `aperas check-links` is a clean pass. Remaining: orchestrator section 7, item 3, still says to document that \"the diff and tests/drift checks were inspected and confirmed clean\", which contradicts the expected drift failure at Step 7. The coder's question about frontmatter units needs no action unless drift lists them as ADDED, and it does not.",
