    "title": "**Resolved — the finished tasks were checked against the graph, and the thread prune did not persist**",
    "text": "**Resolved — the finished tasks were checked against the graph, and the thread prune did not persist**: as [Decision — verify each finished task, then prune](#id/BlockNode:00CVMSSQ68001) set out, each finished task's Reports were matched to the graph before any removal, and these are fully promoted. In `.threads/grapher.md`: the v4 rewrite (the v4 snapshot and milestone), `memory-rules-and-orientation-restructure` and `fold-bottlenecks-dispatch-and-pathing-into-skills` (the v4.1 delta and milestone), `promote-and-fix-subagent-tool-gap` (its resolved issue), `v4.2-progressive-disclosure-refactor` (the v4.2 delta and milestone), `ApeironNgn service reliability` (its issue), `Promote tool gaps to issues` (its five issues) and the empty `tree rendering` heading. In `.threads/coder.md`: `tree rendering` (the rendering decision in `discussion/treeview.md` and the design's tiers), the four v4.x tasks and the two emptied topics. The 15 `aperas remove` calls did not persist, because [a thread write never reaches `.state/` until a view change or a shutdown sweep](../issues/core.md#id/BlockNode:00CVNZXVR8001) and the service they [stalled](../issues/core.md#id/BlockNode:00CVNX6A3R000) was killed. After the restart the removed task roots were live again; three were removed a second time and their content is gone (the v4 rewrite task's blocks, the coder's `ApeironNgn service reliability` topic and the grapher's `tree rendering` topic, whose headings remain), and every other task above is intact and still to be pruned. Kept by decision: this session's tasks, `Record the v3.1 skill edit` and `aperas resolve` in both threads.",
