    "title": "**Observation — the service wedged for over 25 minutes during the grapher's prune, and was killed**",
    "text": "**Observation — the service wedged for over 25 minutes during the grapher's prune, and was killed**: While pruning finished thread tasks with `aperas remove`, the grapher saw the service freeze for 5.4 and about 12 minutes after removing tasks of 42 and 31 live blocks. It then ran `aperas service restart`, which never completed. The old process (pid 220722, about 3.4 hours up) climbed from 4.7 to 5.8 GB resident at roughly 40–50 MB a minute, ran two threads at 100% CPU, wrote nothing, and answered no command, while its lock file said \"ready\" and system memory was down to a few hundred MB free. Its own swapped memory was 26 MB, so it was not swapping. A normal stop (`aperas service stop`) failed after 10 s, and at the user's instruction (\"Just stop it -- clearly stuck!\") the process was killed with SIGKILL at 19:42 after copying the store directory to the scratchpad. A fresh service needed about 60 seconds to answer, was already at 1.5 GB after two minutes, and still dropped commands intermittently while it started.",
