    "title": "**Decision — wait for the fixes before pruning the 12 verified-promoted thread tasks**",
    "text": "**Decision — wait for the fixes before pruning the 12 verified-promoted thread tasks**: (user, answer to a direct question) Re-running `aperas remove` on thread tasks stalled the service again on a fresh process, and thread writes reach `.state/` only through a view operation or shutdown, so the threads stay over the cap until the stall and thread-flush issues are fixed. The grapher's Turn 5 Report holds the list: grapher `memory-rules-and-orientation-restructure`, `promote-and-fix-subagent-tool-gap`, `fold-bottlenecks-dispatch-and-pathing-into-skills`, `v4.2-progressive-disclosure-refactor`, `ApeironNgn service reliability` and `Promote tool gaps to issues`; coder `tree rendering`, the same four v4.x tasks and the `Promote tool gaps to issues` shell.",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00CVKQDJ2G001",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": []
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00CVP855D8002",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "title": "**Decision — the `aperas project` \"changed on disk\" refusal is by design**",
    "text": "**Decision — the `aperas project` \"changed on disk\" refusal is by design**: (user, answer to a direct question) It protects against overwriting an external edit of a projection, so it is not filed as an issue. The 163-block `Record the v3.1 skill edit` task is therefore kept until the prune is possible, and its blocks are not matched against any open issue.",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00CVKQDJ2G001",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": []
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00CVP855D8003",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "title": "**Default — file the `aperas resolve` title-ambiguity defect, keep the coder's `remove-npm-run-and-callouts-from-skills`, and change \"through v4.1\" to \"through v4.3\"**",
    "text": "**Default — file the `aperas resolve` title-ambiguity defect, keep the coder's `remove-npm-run-and-callouts-from-skills`, and change \"through v4.1\" to \"through v4.3\"**: (orchestrator, applying the user's \"promote all issues\", the earlier rule that this session's tasks stay, and the History milestones decision; not yet confirmed by the user) The resolve defect sits only in Freeflow and was hit live (`aperas tree issues/cli.md` is ambiguous with a tombstoned holder), so it is promoted to `issues/core.md`. The coder's task is this session's, so it stays. History's Current Status first sentence moves to v4.3.",
