    "title": "**Decision — fold all node-related persistence into `.state/`**",
    "text": "**Decision — fold all node-related persistence into `.state/`**: (user, confirming the orchestrator's reading with \"Yep\") Any write to a thread-scoped node sets `stateDirty`; the `.state/` divergence stamps cover the thread-partitioned node classes and not only `TreeView`; every flush path writes both mirrors from one rule. A code change on the tools queue, after the skill work; the grapher's issue [thread flush](../issues/core.md#id/BlockNode:00CVNZXVR8001) carries the first part.",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00CVKQDJ2G001",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": [
      "BlockNode:00CVQ1K3P8001"
    ]
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00CVPVT9EG002",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "title": "**Decision — no turn waits more than one minute on something that is not answering**",
    "text": "**Decision — no turn waits more than one minute on something that is not answering**: (user: \"Let's put a time limit on wait... 1 minute! Then fold it into the skill.\") After one minute of waiting, polling or retrying a command, service or process that is not answering, the turn stops, records the trouble as a `**Friction — <topic>**` entry, and ends with a `**Question — <topic>**` to the orchestrator. Folded into v4.3: the base skill states the rule for every role, and the Grapher and Coder skills carry it in their ask-back items. The grapher's 20-minute wait on a pid and its 40-attempt retry wrapper are the cases it rules out.",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00CVKQDJ2G001",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": []
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00CVPVT9EG003",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "title": "**Note — a fresh service needs about a minute to answer**",
    "text": "**Note — a fresh service needs about a minute to answer**: (orchestrator) After the kill, the new service took about 60 seconds to answer its first command, then dropped commands intermittently for a few minutes more. The rule's one-minute limit therefore applies to waiting on a stalled command or service, and a subagent that finds the service down ends its turn instead of restarting it. The orchestrator, which owns the service, is the one that restarts it. Not yet confirmed by the user.",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00CVKQDJ2G001",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": []
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00CVPVT9EG004",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "title": "**Open — the second half of the candidate wording**",
    "text": "**Open — the second half of the candidate wording**: (orchestrator) A command that discards or restarts shared state (`aperas service restart`, `aperas reload --discard`, a kill) ends the turn with a Question instead of running. The user confirmed the one-minute limit only, so this half waits for an answer.",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00CVKQDJ2G001",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": []
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00CVPWZ06R001",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "title": "**Verification — the one-minute wait rule inspected and confirmed**",
    "text": "**Verification — the one-minute wait rule inspected and confirmed**: (orchestrator) The rule is in the base skill (Core Thread Disciplines, after \"Ask back instead of guessing\"), the Coder skill (Operational Invariants) and the Grapher skill (a `Rule` line at the end of section 1, since that skill has no ask-back item; the placement is accepted). Each says no turn waits, polls or retries more than one minute in total on a command, service or process that is not answering, then records a `Friction` entry and ends with a `Question`, and that a subagent finding the service down ends its turn and does not restart it. The discard-or-restart half is not added. `skill_drift.py` exits 1 with 3 ADDED but unrecorded (base Core Thread Disciplines, Coder section 5, Grapher section 1), 0 Status and 0 DROPPED, and `aperas check-links` is a clean pass. The coder's friction was a fresh-service answer that came after 20 seconds, which it waited out without restarting.",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00CVKQDJ2G001",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": []
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00CVPXK90G001",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "title": "### aperas — Core Thread Disciplines, One minute is the limit",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00CVJXQWNG001",
    "type": "heading",
    "children": [
      "BlockNode:00CVPXK90G002"
    ]
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00CVPXK90G002",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "props": [
      {
        "@id": "BlockNode:00CVPXK90G002:props:StringProp:00CVPXKH3G000",
        "@type": "StringProp",
        "key": "orderedList",
        "value": "false"
      },
      {
        "@id": "BlockNode:00CVPXK90G002:props:StringProp:00CVPXKH3G001",
        "@type": "StringProp",
        "key": "startIndex",
        "value": "1"
      }
    ],
    "title": "**One minute is the limit on anything that does not answer, for every role**",
    "text": "**One minute is the limit on anything that does not answer, for every role**: No agent waits, polls or retries more than one minute in total on a command, service or process that is not answering. After that minute it stops trying harder and reports to its upline: a subagent records the trouble as a `**Friction — <topic>**` entry and ends its turn with a `**Question — <topic>**` to the orchestrator; the orchestrator reports to the user, and may keep waiting only after telling the user. The orientation is to not try hard on something that seems stuck and to bubble it up. A subagent that finds the service down ends its turn and does not restart it, because the orchestrator owns the service; a restart or kill of the service is for the user to approve.",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00CVPXK90G001",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": []
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00CVPXK90G003",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "title": "### aperas-coder — Operational Invariants, Never wait on a silent command",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00CVJXQWNG001",
    "type": "heading",
    "children": [
      "BlockNode:00CVPXK90G004"
    ]
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00CVPXK90G004",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "props": [
      {
        "@id": "BlockNode:00CVPXK90G004:props:StringProp:00CVPXKH3R000",
        "@type": "StringProp",
        "key": "orderedList",
        "value": "false"
      },
      {
        "@id": "BlockNode:00CVPXK90G004:props:StringProp:00CVPXKH3R001",
        "@type": "StringProp",
        "key": "startIndex",
        "value": "1"
      }
    ],
    "title": "**Never wait on a silent command beyond one minute**",
    "text": "**Never wait on a silent command beyond one minute**: If a command, the service or a test run does not answer, wait, poll or retry no more than one minute in total, then record a `**Friction — <topic>**` entry and end the turn with a `**Question — <topic>**`. If the service is down, end the turn and do not restart it; the orchestrator owns the service.",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00CVPXK90G003",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": []
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00CVPXK90R000",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "title": "### aperas-grapher — Every Invocation, Never wait on a silent command",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00CVJXQWNG001",
    "type": "heading",
    "children": [
      "BlockNode:00CVPXK90R001"
    ]
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00CVPXK90R001",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "title": "00CVPXK90R001",
    "text": "> **Rule**: Never wait on a silent command beyond one minute. If a graph command, the service or a projection does not answer, wait, poll or retry no more than one minute in total, then record a `**Friction — <topic>**` entry and end the turn with a `**Question — <topic>**`. If the service is down, end the turn and do not restart it; the orchestrator owns the service.",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00CVPXK90R000",
    "type": "blockquote",
    "children": []
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00CVPZKPN8000",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "title": "**Decision — the one-minute rule applies to every agent, including the orchestrator, and the orientation is to bubble up**",
    "text": "**Decision — the one-minute rule applies to every agent, including the orchestrator, and the orientation is to bubble up**: (user: \"The 1min rules applies to all agents, if the Orchestrator waits longer, it must report to user. The general orientation is: don't try hard on a thing seemingly stuck, just bubble up to the upline.\") After one minute of waiting, polling or retrying something that is not answering, an agent reports to its upline instead of trying harder: a subagent ends its turn with a `**Question — <topic>**` to the orchestrator, and the orchestrator reports to the user, and may keep waiting only after telling the user. This replaces the orchestrator's earlier plan of a longer limit for service start and supersedes the unconfirmed note that the orchestrator restarts the service on its own. The wording of the base skill, which now says \"to the orchestrator\", and a line in the orchestrator skill need updating; queued as a coder edit after the grapher's current turn, so the delta is updated once.",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00CVKQDJ2G001",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": []
  },
