    ],
    "title": "**`aperas resolve`'s title-ambiguity check does not filter tombstoned candidates, so a dead holder makes a live path read as ambiguous**",
    "text": "**`aperas resolve`'s title-ambiguity check does not filter tombstoned candidates, so a dead holder makes a live path read as ambiguous**: reproduced 2026-10-02: `aperas tree issues/cli.md` fails with `'cli.md' is ambiguous among: ArtifactNode:00CF2AEA78000 (\"cli.md\"), ArtifactNode:00CF1TZQV8000 (\"cli.md\")`, where the second id is a tombstoned holder, while `aperas tree issues/core.md` resolves. First seen when the thin `cli.md` docs were created. Cause, read from the code: `findChild(text)` (`node.ts:479-490`) builds its `candidates` array from `this.treeChildren` filtering only on `title !== undefined`, never on `tombstonedAt`, and `BlockNode.treeChildren` and `FolderNode.treeChildren` (`node.ts:513-515`, `1143-1145`) return `this.children ?? []` with no liveness filter at any layer above, so a tombstoned sibling with a matching title lands in both the exact-slug match and the prefix-slug fallback and can make an otherwise unique live title ambiguous. `findChild` is one shared method on `TreeNode`, called from exactly two places, `resolve.ts:116` (`aperas resolve`) and `resolveCreate.ts:164` (`aperas resolve --create-holder`), each once per deep-path segment, so one filter covers both commands, and every command that resolves a bare path (`tree`, `show`, `project`, `insert`) inherits the failure. Fix to try: filter `candidates` in `findChild` to exclude any child with `tombstonedAt` set before either slug match runs, using the same idiom as [the `diffChildren` fix](../issues/core.md#id/BlockNode:00CF1WZ4JG004) (`isLiveOld` in `reconcile.ts`) and [the dead-container fix](../issues/core.md#id/BlockNode:00CF1WZ4JG006) (`tombstoneVacuousContainers`). Workaround: resolve the live node by ID, or by a path that does not end on the ambiguous title. Not yet fixed; no coder task is open for it. Filed 2026-10-02.",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00CF1WZ4JG002",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": []
  },
