    "title": "**Resolved — the one-minute rule is recorded in the v4.3 delta, the lead-ins are rewritten, and the Turn 6 filings are done**",
    "text": "**Resolved — the one-minute rule is recorded in the v4.3 delta, the lead-ins are rewritten, and the Turn 6 filings are done**: the delta gained three entries for the rule's added units, one each in the base Core Thread Disciplines, the Coder's Operational Invariants and the Grapher's Every Invocation, and `skill_drift.py` exits 0 with 0 Status, 0 added and 0 dropped findings. The rule's wording is recorded as the files stand now; the queued coder edit that widens it to every agent will supersede these entries. All 53 entries of the old shape `**Term** (qualifier): body` under the five Freeflow headings of this task were rewritten to `**Term**: (qualifier) body` with `aperas update --text-only` (the count of about 44 in the lead-in decision predates later entries, and two entries whose bold span holds a nested `**` needed a second pass), and [the lead-in title issue](../issues/linking.md#id/BlockNode:00CVMYB5W0001) records the convention as chosen and the engine option as open. The `aperas resolve` defect is filed as [its own issue](../issues/core.md#id/BlockNode:00CVQ0PVS0001), the link-sweep lead went onto [the removal-stall issue](../issues/core.md#id/BlockNode:00CVNX6A3R000), the routing mismatch, the history and the three-part fix went onto [the thread-flush issue](../issues/core.md#id/BlockNode:00CVNZXVR8001), and History's Current Status now reads \"through v4.3\".",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00CVKQDJ2G001",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": []
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00CVQ2HDJ0001",
