      }
    ],
    "title": "**Finding — the service's memory is a serious problem in two parts**",
    "text": "**Finding — the service's memory is a serious problem in two parts**: (user: \"Such a constant growth and the 5GB size is a serious thing.\") First, the old service (pid 220722, up from 16:16) reached 4.74 GB at 19:20 and 5.76 GB at 19:42, a rise of roughly 40–50 MB a minute over the last hour, with two threads at 100% CPU, almost no disk writes, and a 2.1 GB V8 heap limit that its resident size is far above, so most of it sits outside the V8 heap. Second, a fresh service idles at 1.05–1.5 GB (median 1.34 GB, maximum 2.18 GB) over 379 samples and 63 minutes, while the whole graph on disk is 3.66 MB of JSON-LD, about 37,000 quads; that is roughly 350 times the data size at rest. The fresh one did not grow over that hour under light use and light load from the grapher's updates, so the 5 GB climb needs heavier work (the thread-task removals, and a long uptime) than the sampler has seen.",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00CVKQDJ2G001",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": [
      "BlockNode:00CVQ510HR001"
    ]
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00CVQ2HDJ0002",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "links": [
      {
        "@id": "BlockNode:00CVQ2HDJ0002:links:Link:00CVQ74E1R000",
        "@type": "Link",
