          }
        ]
      }
    ],
    "title": "**Decision — promote the memory problem to an issue in the next Filing turn**",
    "text": "**Decision — promote the memory problem to an issue in the next Filing turn**: (orchestrator, applying the user's \"promote all issues\"; not yet confirmed) `issues/core.md` gets a defect entry for the 5 GB growth and the 1.3 GB idle size, linked to the removal-stall issue [removal stall](../issues/core.md#id/BlockNode:00CVNX6A3R000) and the verify-slowdown issues, with the numbers above and the measurements still to take. It goes in after the grapher's current turn so the issue docs are touched once.",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00CVKQDJ2G001",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": [
      "BlockNode:00CVQ53B28001"
    ]
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00CVQ32E68001",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "title": "**Verification — the grapher's Turn 6 filing inspected and confirmed**",
    "text": "**Verification — the grapher's Turn 6 filing inspected and confirmed**: (orchestrator) `skill_drift.py` exits 0 from `Aperas/` (0 Status, 0 ADDED, 0 DROPPED, 192 accounted for) and `aperas check-links` is a clean pass. The Report, the `aperas resolve` defect in `issues/core.md` and the grapher's `Resolved` entry exist, and none of the 75 children of the Freeflow heading now has an id as its title. The grapher rewrote 53 entries, not the 44 first counted, because later entries were added and two nested-bold ones needed a second pass. It stayed inside the one-minute rule: no stall, no restart, no `reload --discard`, no `remove`. Its two questions are answered: the orchestrator fixed the stale count in the lead-in Decision itself, and the three one-minute entries in the delta are updated in place after the queued coder edit widens the rule.",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00CVKQDJ2G001",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": []
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00CVQ40XN8001",
