    "title": "**Decision — the slow-service investigation goes first on the tools queue, ahead of the `check-links` fix**",
    "text": "**Decision — the slow-service investigation goes first on the tools queue, ahead of the `check-links` fix**: (user: \"Yep. Not only mem, but the whole issue of the slow service.\") One investigation covers every symptom of the service being slow or large, not memory alone: [the removal stall](../issues/core.md#id/BlockNode:00CVNX6A3R000), [the spurious \"not running\"](../issues/core.md#id/BlockNode:00CVMPABY8001), [the memory size and growth](#id/BlockNode:00CVQ2HDJ0001) (the issue is filed in the grapher's Turn 7), [the process-lifetime slowdown that split `verify`](../issues/core.md#id/BlockNode:00CJ0202MG001) and [its open \"why isolation helps\"](../issues/core.md#id/BlockNode:00CJ0HX2Y0000), the whole-artifact link sweeps around every write, the 60-second start, and the idle size. Related, in the same area but about persistence: [the thread-flush gap](../issues/core.md#id/BlockNode:00CVNZXVR8001) and [tombstoned thread nodes leaking into the tracked mirror](../issues/treeview.md#id/BlockNode:00CVNX6YD0001). The `check-links` dangling-target fix stays queued behind it.",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00CVKQDJ2G001",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": []
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00CVQ5E7V8002",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "title": "**Finding — the orchestrator cited block ids as bare code, which creates no link**",
    "text": "**Finding — the orchestrator cited block ids as bare code, which creates no link**: (user: \"Why did you use codes, e.g. `verify-slowdown issue (BlockNode:00CJ0202MG001)`, instead of wikilinks?\") Under the five Freeflow headings of the v4.3 work, 11 of 149 entries mention a `BlockNode:` id as plain text, 14 mentions in all, and the chat summaries do the same. A bare id gives no backlink, cannot be followed in the graph, and cannot be checked by `aperas check-links`, so the claim has no provenance; the orchestrator skill already says to cite by wikilink. The orchestrator wrote the ids in a hurry because a link needs the artifact path and the anchor form. Those 11 entries are converted to wikilinks after the grapher's Turn 7, which is editing the same document, and every new entry uses `[title](path#id/BlockNode:…)`.",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00CVKQDJ2G001",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": []
  },
