    "title": "**Verification — the grapher's Turn 7 closing filing inspected and confirmed**",
    "text": "**Verification — the grapher's Turn 7 closing filing inspected and confirmed**: (orchestrator) `skill_drift.py` exits 0 from `Aperas/` bare, with `--added` and with `--dropped` (0 Status, 0 ADDED, 0 DROPPED, 192 accounted for) and `aperas check-links` is a clean pass. The delta entry for the one-minute rule is updated in place and the \"Stuck Things Go to the User\" callout has its own entry. [The service-memory issue](../issues/core.md#id/BlockNode:00CVQ4Z968001) is filed in `issues/core.md` with its three `Promoted to` backlinks, History's v4.3 milestone covers everything v4.3 shipped, and the Threads and Roles blocks of the design each gained a sentence on the bounded wait and the user as the orchestrator's upline. The grapher stayed inside the one-minute rule: two spurious \"not running\" answers, each cleared by one retry, nothing restarted.",
