    "title": "**Decision — links flow compat → ingest → canon → project → compat**",
    "text": "**Decision — links flow compat → ingest → canon → project → compat**: (user: \"as the design has clearly separated, canon inside (graph use) and compat outside (projected artifacts), and the conversion at the boundary. So, compat -[ingest]-> canon -[project]-> compat is the ideal flow, which has not been done.\") Inside the graph a reference is a canonical address and the writer, through the CLI, never has to type a path or an anchor; in a projected artifact the same reference is the MD-compatible link, relative path and anchor, generated from the target's current location. The first conversion belongs to ingest and the second to projection. Today both directions are missing: a node's stored text still holds the compat form (`[title](../design/x.md#id/BlockNode:…)`), which is why the skills' templates teach it and why a renamed or moved artifact breaks every compat link that points at it. This replaces the earlier open question about what the authoring fix should be and is [the design in `design/linking.md`](../design/linking.md#id/BlockNode:00CDBYV4T0001) carried through. Promoted to an issue at the next Filing turn.",
