    "title": "**Decision — the scratch removal run is approved, and the instrumentation and sampler take the recommended shape**",
    "text": "**Decision — the scratch removal run is approved, and the instrumentation and sampler take the recommended shape**: (user: \"OK, yes for all the 3.\", answering the orchestrator's three questions) First, the coder may run one scratch measurement of the removal path: a script in `/tmp` that rehydrates a copy of the store in its own process, times `runRemove` and its pre- and post-sweeps step by step in memory, never writes to the graph, has a 60-second limit and is deleted afterwards. Second, the service's in-process instrumentation goes in a new `apeironNgn/serviceDiagnostics.ts` behind `APERAS_DIAGNOSTICS=1`, read by `spawnService`, which also adds `--heapsnapshot-signal` and `--diagnostic-dir` when it is set, with everything written through `logService`. Third, the sampler stays Python in `monorepo/packages/cli/diagnostics/` with a `svc:sample` script, gains a once-a-second raw-socket ping that keeps the failure text, `VmHWM`, `/proc/pid/io` and mirror-file sizes, configurable paths and no one-minute client probe. These answer [the open question on where the instrumentation goes](../discussion/aperas-skill.md#id/BlockNode:00CVQFC3SR002); the user confirmed the shape, and a written design is reviewed before any change to `service.ts`.",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00CVKQDJ2G001",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": []
  },
  {
