    ],
    "title": "**Decision — the orchestrator skill's Harness Tool Mappings stop telling the old story**",
    "text": "**Decision — the orchestrator skill's Harness Tool Mappings stop telling the old story**: (user: \"update the skill where it still tells the old story: Harness Tool Mappings: Claude Code's `SendMessage` is now equivalent to Antigravity's `send_message`.\") The Claude Code line says \"Call `Task` for every turn (inherently ephemeral and stateless)\", which was true of the Task tool before [`SendMessage` was retargeted to subagents](#id/BlockNode:00CVRB63Z0000). It becomes: call `Agent` (the tool formerly named `Task`) for every turn, and never use `SendMessage` across distinct turns, because it resumes a finished subagent with its whole conversation, which is what `send_message` does in Antigravity. The \"Preventing Transcript Bloat\" bullet names `SendMessage` beside `send_message`. A note to a running subagent within the same turn is fine and arrives between its tool calls, and the way a subagent asks the orchestrator for anything that cannot wait is still to end its turn with a `Question`. The edit goes through the Coder; whether it is a patch to v4.3, which is committed in the code repo but not in the graph repo, or a v4.4 bump is the user's choice.",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00CVKQDJ2G001",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": []
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00CVRTX3WG001",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "title": "**Decision — patch v4.3, not v4.4**",
    "text": "**Decision — patch v4.3, not v4.4**: (user: \"Patch v4.3\") The Harness Tool Mappings correction is a patch to v4.3: the `Status:` lines stay at v4.3, the Grapher updates the v4.3 delta in place, and the user commits the follow-up.",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00CVKQDJ2G001",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": []
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00CVRVYV00001",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "title": "**Verification — the Harness Tool Mappings patch inspected and confirmed**",
    "text": "**Verification — the Harness Tool Mappings patch inspected and confirmed**: (orchestrator) The orchestrator skill's two lines now say that `SendMessage` in Claude Code, like `send_message` in Antigravity, is how a session gets reused, and that the Claude Code line is to call `Agent` (formerly `Task`) every turn and never `SendMessage` across distinct turns, with a note to a running subagent within a turn allowed. The diff is 2 insertions and 2 deletions in one file, the `.claude/skills` and `.agents/skills` paths being symlinks to it, and `Status:` stays v4.3. `skill_drift.py` exits 1 as expected with 2 ADDED (the Preventing Transcript Bloat bullet and the Claude Code mapping bullet) and 2 DROPPED (their old versions), 0 Status; `aperas check-links` is a clean pass.",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00CVKQDJ2G001",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": []
  },
